h Goa Tour\r\n* All road transfers for sightseeing\r\n* All taxes','* Entry fees are not included in the cost.\r\n* Anything that is not mentioned in inclusions.\r\n','Rates are valid till 22nd October, 2022','2022-12-26','2022-12-30',0,0,0,'2022-10-20 14:05:30','2022-10-20 14:05:30'),(182,501,349,2,0,0,0,0,'Dubai Adventure','4 Nights stay in Dubai with breakfast\r\n\r\n','','* DELHI-DUBAI AND DUBAI-DELHI FLIGHT FARE\r\n* RETURN AIRPORT TRANSFERS ON PVT BASIS\r\n* 4 NIGHTS STAY IN ABOVE MENTIONED 4 STAR HOTEL \r\n* DAILY BREAKFAST\r\n* CITY TOUR HALF-DAY SIC\r\n* DESERT SAFARI WITH BBQ DINNER SIC\r\n* MARINA DHOW CRUISE SIC\r\n* BURJ KHALIFA WITH 124TH LEVEL NP SIC','ANYTHING THAT IS NOT MENTIONED IN INCLUSIONS','','2022-11-25','2022-11-29',1,0,0,'2022-10-20 15:43:32','2022-10-20 15:47:56'),(183,502,15518,2,1,1,65400,17000,'Scenic Kerala','8N/9D Tour of Kerala\r\n\r\n2N Kovalam - 1N Alleppey - 1N Thekkady - 2N Munnar - 1N Kochi - 1N Calicut\r\n\r\nDay 1: Trivandrum Arrival to Kovalam\r\nArrival Transfer - Trivandrum - Kovalam Arrival\r\nCheck-in at Hotel. Overnight stay at Kovalam.\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 2: Kanyakymari to Kovalam\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel \r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Kovalam – Trivandrum – Kovalam\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed for Sightseeing. Visit Padmanabha Swami Temple, Kuthiramalika \r\nPalace Museum, Zoo, Napier  Museum & Veli Tourist Village. Overnight stay at Kovalam.\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 3: Kovalam to Alleppey\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel \r\nTransfers - Kovalam to Alleppey\r\nVisit Alleppey beach, sunset and enjoy shopping if staying in Alleppey. Visit Alleppey Beach and Backwaters. Enjoy all the amenities of this hotel/resort for a day which includes fishing in the backwaters (depending on the hotel/resort selected). Overnight stay at the hotel/resort\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 4: Alleppey - Thekkady\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel \r\nTransfers - Alleppey - Thekkady\r\nThekkady is a world-famous wildlife sanctuary. On arrival check-in at Hotel. In the Afternoon, \r\nvisit the wildlife sanctuary & enjoy the boating (tickets charges are extra and subject to availability). Visit spice plantations. The evening will be free for the Cultural show \r\n(Kathakali & Kalaripayattu on direct payment) & local shopping. Overnight Stay at Hotel.\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 5: Thekady to Munnar\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel \r\nTransfers - Thekkady to Munnar\r\nOn the way visit Valara, Cheeyappara waterfalls & Tea Plantations. Check-in at the Hotel. Afternoon visit Rajamala, the best place to see Nilgiri Tahr (Hermitragus Hilarious) - the mountain goat of South India & Tea Museum. In the evening, have a short visit to Munnar town. You can see the \r\nbeautiful tea estates like a green paradise. Overnight stay at Munnar.\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 6: Munnar Sightseeing DAY 02\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel\r\n\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Munnar Sightseeing DAY 02\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed to enjoy a full day sightseeing tour of Munnar. Rose Garden, Tea Garden, Photo Point, Madupetty Dam/Lake, Echo Point & Kundala Dam/Lake. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 7: Munnar to Cochin\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - \r\nTransfers - Munnar to Cochin\r\nCheck in at the hotel. Proceed for Cochin sightseeing. Visit the Dutch Palace. Jewish Synagogue - built in 1568 and the oldest Synagogue in the Commonwealth are at Mattancherry. St. Francis Church - built in 1510 and the oldest European church in India, Chinese Fishing Nets- introduced by the court of Kublai Khan can be seen in Fort Cochin. Fort Cochin Beach etc. Overnight stay at Cochin\r\n \r\n\r\nDay 8: Cochin - Calicut\r\nMorning after breakfast check out and proceed to Calicut. The central Kozhikode/Calicut Beach, overlooked by an old lighthouse, is a popular spot for watching the sunset. Inland, tree-lined Mananchira Square, with its musical fountain, surrounds the massive Mananchira Tank, an artificial pond. The Stone Memorial for Vasco de Gama stands tall in honor of the Portuguese explorer who \r\nlanded on Indian soil. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 9: Pick-up from the venue (mentioned by the client) and drop at Calicut Airport.\r\n\r\n','','1. Delhi to Trivandrum and Calicut to Delhi Airfare\r\n2. 7 Nights stay in above-mentioned hotels/resorts.\r\n3. Meal plans as indicated on the itinerary\r\n4. All Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\n5. All Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost included','Anything that is not mentioned in the inclusions.','','2022-11-26','2022-12-04',1,0,0,'2022-10-27 18:49:59','2022-10-28 22:01:55'),(184,504,15518,2,1,1,83500,18500,'Scenic Kerala','8N/9D Tour of Kerala\r\n\r\n2N Kovalam - 1N Alleppey - 1N Thekkady - 2N Munnar - 1N Kochi - 1N Calicut\r\n\r\nDay 1: Trivandrum Arrival to Kovalam\r\nArrival Transfer - Trivandrum - Kovalam Arrival\r\nCheck-in at Hotel. Overnight stay at Kovalam.\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 2: Kovalam Sightseeing\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel \r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Kovalam – Trivandrum – Kovalam\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed for Sightseeing. Visit Padmanabha Swami Temple, Kuthiramalika \r\nPalace Museum, Zoo, Napier  Museum & Veli Tourist Village. Overnight stay at Kovalam.\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 3: Kovalam to Alleppey\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel \r\nTransfers - Kovalam to Alleppey\r\nVisit Alleppey beach, sunset and enjoy shopping if staying in Alleppey. Visit Alleppey Beach and Backwaters. Enjoy all the amenities of this hotel/resort for a day which includes fishing in the backwaters (depending on the hotel/resort selected). Overnight stay at the hotel/resort\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 4: Alleppey - Thekkady\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel \r\nTransfers - Alleppey - Thekkady\r\nThekkady is a world-famous wildlife sanctuary. On arrival check-in at Hotel. In the Afternoon, \r\nvisit the wildlife sanctuary & enjoy the boating (tickets charges are extra and subject to availability). Visit spice plantations. The evening will be free for the Cultural show \r\n(Kathakali & Kalaripayattu on direct payment) & local shopping. Overnight Stay at Hotel.\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 5: Thekady to Munnar\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel \r\nTransfers - Thekkady to Munnar\r\nOn the way visit Valara, Cheeyappara waterfalls & Tea Plantations. Check-in at the Hotel. Afternoon visit Rajamala, the best place to see Nilgiri Tahr (Hermitragus Hilarious) - the mountain goat of South India & Tea Museum. In the evening, have a short visit to Munnar town. You can see the \r\nbeautiful tea estates like a green paradise. Overnight stay at Munnar.\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 6: Munnar Sightseeing DAY 02\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel\r\n\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Munnar Sightseeing DAY 02\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed to enjoy a full day sightseeing tour of Munnar. Rose Garden, Tea Garden, Photo Point, Madupetty Dam/Lake, Echo Point & Kundala Dam/Lake. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 7: Munnar to Cochin\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - \r\nTransfers - Munnar to Cochin\r\nCheck in at the hotel. Proceed for Cochin sightseeing. Visit the Dutch Palace. Jewish Synagogue - built in 1568 and the oldest Synagogue in the Commonwealth are at Mattancherry. St. Francis Church - built in 1510 and the oldest European church in India, Chinese Fishing Nets- introduced by the court of Kublai Khan can be seen in Fort Cochin. Fort Cochin Beach etc. Overnight stay at Cochin\r\n \r\n\r\nDay 8: Cochin - Calicut\r\nMorning after breakfast check out and proceed to Calicut. The central Kozhikode/Calicut Beach, overlooked by an old lighthouse, is a popular spot for watching the sunset. Inland, tree-lined Mananchira Square, with its musical fountain, surrounds the massive Mananchira Tank, an artificial pond. The Stone Memorial for Vasco de Gama stands tall in honor of the Portuguese explorer who \r\nlanded on Indian soil. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 9: Pick-up from the venue (mentioned by the client) followed by visit to Baypore Beach, Kappad beach, Kozhikode beach, Mittayi Theruvu, Krishna Menon art gallery and museum. 