noon visit Rajamala (Eravikulam National Park - open as per the directions by the forest authorities ), the best place to see Nilgiri Tahr (Hermitragus Hilarious) - the mountain goat of South India & Tea Museum.  Evening have a short visit at Munnar town. You can see the beautiful tea estates like a green paradise. Overnight stay at Munnar.\r\n\r\nDay 2: Munnar Sightseeing\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed to enjoy full day sight seeing tour of Munnar. Rose Garden, Tea Garden, Photo Point, Madupetty Dam/Lake, Echo Point & Kundala Dam/Lake. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\n\r\nDay 3: Munnar to Thekkady transfer\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Thekkady .Thekkady is a world famous wildlife sanctuary and it is also called as Periyar. On arrival check in at Hotel. Afternoon visit wildlife sanctuary & enjoy the boating ( tickets charges are extra and subject to availability ). Visit spice plantations. Apart from being enjoyable these plantation tours gives tourists an insight into the growing, harvesting and processing of spices. Evening will be free for Cultural show ( Kathakali & Kalaripayattu on direct payment ) & local shopping. Overnight stay at Thekkady.\r\n\r\nDay 4: Thekkady to Alleppey Transfer\r\nMorning after breakfast, check out and proceed to Alleppey (House Boat) Check in 12.00 noon and Enjoy the backwaters, scenery and different places for 21hrs in Kerala Style House boats from 12Noon. Observe the daily life of peoples who lives near the lake/canal while cruising. In the houseboat you will be greeted with welcome drink. Lunch, Dinner and breakfast will be provided as per the timming. Evening Tea/Coffee & snacks will be provided. Overnight stay in the houseboat.\"\r\n\r\nDay 5: Alleppey to Kovalam Transfer\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel Houseboat and transfer to Kovalam. Check in at Hotel. Kovalam is an evergreen and pleasant climatic beach. Kovalam is a dreamland for tourists all over the world. With high rock promontory and a calm bay of blue waters, this beach paradise creates a unique aquarelle on moonlit nights. Kovalam was brought to the public eye by the Maharaja of Travancore. Over the past three decades, the place has been well developed, and now figures prominently on the world tourism map. Overnight stay at Kovalam.\r\n\r\nDay 6: Kovalam Sightseeing\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed for Sightseeing. Visit Padmanabha Swami Temple, Kuthiramalika Palace Museum, Zoo, Napier  Museum & Veli Tourist Village. Overnight stay at Kovalam.\r\n\r\nDay 7: Kovalam to Trivandrum Airport\r\nMorning after breakfast check out the Hotel and drive towards the Trivandrum Airport/Railway station for your onward journey. Tour ends with happy memories.','','* Delhi to Kochi and Trivandrum to Delhi Flight Fare\r\n* Meal plans as indicated on the itinerary\r\n* Accommodation on Twin Sharing Basis\r\n* All Inclusion and sightseeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\n* All Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Costs\r\n','* All those which are not mentioned above\r\n* Visa charges\r\n* Travel insurance\r\n* Entry Fees To Monuments And Palaces\r\n* Porterage At Hotels And Airports, Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Liquors, Wine, Etc\r\n* All Items Of Personal Nature\r\n* Any Cost Arising Due To Natural Calamities Like Landslides, Roadblocks, Etc\r\n* Any Increase In Taxes Or Fuel Leading To An Increase In Surface Transport\r\n* Ayurveda Charges\r\n* Only Non Ac Rooms Are Provided In Munnar And Thekkady As They Are Hill Stations\r\n* Mandatory X- Mas / New Year Eve Supplementary Charges , That Should Be Paid By The Guest Directly To The Hotels Concerned.','The Rates are valid till 20th November, 2022\r\n','2023-01-02','2023-01-08',1,0,0,'2022-11-17 22:19:02','2022-11-17 22:19:02'),(197,533,349,4,0,0,55500,18000,'Amazing Dubai','Dubai Package (5 Nights 6 Days) ','','RETURN AIRPORT TRANSFERS - PVT Transfer\r\nDubai CITY ORIENTATION TOUR  - SIC Transfer\r\nDESERT SAFARI BBQ DINNER  - SIC Transfer\r\nMARINA DHOW CRUISE WITH DINNER - SIC Transfer\r\nBURJ KHALIFA 124TH LEVEL NP - PVT TRANSFER\r\nDUBAI FRAME PVT Transfer\r\n','- Tourism Dirham is not included in above quotation and shall be directly payable by the guest.\r\n- OTB charges if applicable.\r\n- Anything not mentioned in inclusions. ','','2023-01-26','2023-01-31',1,0,0,'2022-11-21 12:38:18','2022-11-21 12:38:18'),(198,534,349,2,0,0,31000,10000,'Amazing Dubai','Amazing Dubai 6 N 7 Days','','ACCOMODATION AS PER OPTION SELECTED. \r\nRETURN AIRPORT TRANSFERS - PVT TRANSFER\r\nDubai CITY ORIENTATION TOUR - SIC TRANSFER \r\nDESERT SAFARI BBQ DINNER  - SIC TRANSFER\r\nMARINA DHOW CRUISE WITH DINNER  - SIC TRANSFER\r\nBURJ KHALIFA 124TH LEVEL NP - SIC TRANSFER\r\nABU DHABI CITY TOUR - SIC TRANSFER\r\n','- Tourism Dirham is not included in above quotation and shall be directly payable by the guest.\r\n- OTB Charges if applicable.\r\n- Anything not mentioned in inclusions. ','','2022-12-15','2022-12-21',0,0,0,'2022-11-21 13:01:33','2022-11-21 13:13:20'),(199,535,349,2,1,0,82100,24000,'Amazing UAE','Dubai Tour Package','','Transfers from Dubai Airport to Abu Dhabi Hotel – PVT \r\nTransfers from Abu Dhabi Hotel to Dubai Hotel – PVT \r\nTransfers from Dubai Hotel to Dubai Airport – PVT \r\nDubai City Tour – SIC \r\nDesert Safari with BBQ Dinner – SIC \r\nMarina Dhow Cruise with Dinner – SIC \r\nAquaventure with Lost Chamber – SIC \r\n1 Day 2 Park Pass (Yas Water World / Ferrari & Warner Bros) – Ticket Only \r\n\r\n','- Tourism Dirham is not included in above quotation and shall be directly payable by the guest.\r\nAnything not mentioned in Inclusions. ','','2022-12-13','2022-12-20',0,0,0,'2022-11-21 15:39:25','2022-11-21 15:53:02'),(200,536,13540,4,0,0,100800,16000,'Mesmerizing North East','3N Shillong - 2N Guwahati\r\n\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n1st Day - (Sunday 25th December) : Guwahati Airport / Rly Station to Shillong - Transfer\r\n\r\nApprox Distance: 100 Km • Est. Travel Time: 3 hours\r\n\r\nOn arrival at Guwahati Airport / Railway Station & transfer to Shillong, which is also called the \'Scotland of the East\". On the way visit the majestic Umium Lake (Barapani). You may do the water sports here (Optional). On arrival at Shillong, check in at your hotel. Evening you can visit Police Bazaar which is the biggest local market. Overnight stay at Shillong.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n2nd Day - (Monday 26th December) : Shillong to Cherrapunjee - Excursion\r\n\r\nApprox Distance: 60 Km • Est. Travel Time: 2 hours\r\n\r\nAfter early breakfast drive to Cherrapunjee (4,400 ft.), the wettest place in the world. You will see the beautiful waterfall known as Nohkalikai. You can also explore the caves known as Mawsmai. Evening return to Shillong, enroute visit Elephanta falls. Overnight stay at Shillong.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n3rd Day - (Tuesday 27th December) : Shillong to Mawlynnong and Dawki - Excursion\r\n\r\nApprox Distance: 120 Km • Est. Travel Time: 4 hours\r\n\r\nAfter early breakfast drive to Mawlynnong – “Asia’s Cleanest Village”. Mawlynnong offers many interesting sights such as the living root bridge and another strange natural phenomenon of a boulder balancing on another small rock. Later proceed to Dawki, a small town near India Bangladesh border. Enjoy breathtaking view of the Umangot River. Evening drive back to Shillong. Stay overnight at your hotel in Shillong.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n4th Day - (Wednesday 28th December) : Shillong to Guwahati - Sightseeing and Transfer\r\n\r\nApprox Distance: 100 Km • Est. Travel Time: 3 hours\r\n\r\nAfter breakfast check out from hotel and visit Don Bosco Museum (Sunday Closed) & Ward’s Lake. After that drive to Guwahati. Arrive and check in at your hotel. In evening we suggest an optional tour of Golden sunset cruise on the Brahmaputra (Direct Payment by own). Overnight stay at Guwahati.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n5th Day - (Thursday 29th December) : Guwahati - Local Sightseeing\r\n\r\nAfter breakfast out to visit Kamakhya Temple (Notes: Timing 08:00 A.M till 01:00 P.M & 3:00 P.M till its gets dark), Tirupati Balaji Temple, Nabagraha Temple, Assam State Museum (Closed on Monday), State Zoo cum Botanical Garden, Regional Science Centre and Sukreswar Temple (The 6th Jyotirlinga of Shiva). Evening you may take a River Cruise (Direct Payment) on the mighty River Brahmaputra. Overnight stay at Guwahati.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n6th Day - (Friday 30th December) : Guwahati Hotel to Guwahati Airport / Rly Station - Transfer\r\n\r\nAfter breakfast check out from hotel & transfer to Guwahati Airport / Railway Station for your onward journey.\r\n\r\n','','• Delhi to Guwahati and Guwahati to Delhi Airfare\r\n• Transportation\r\n\r\n• Accommodation as mentioned in hotel section\r\n\r\n• Meal Plan (as mentioned above)\r\n\r\n• Exclusive AC vehicle for transfers & sightseeing. (AC will not run in hill area)\r\n\r\n• All hotel taxes (as per itinerary)\r\n\r\n• Rates are valid for INDIAN NATIONALS only','• Personal Expenses such as Laundry, telephone calls, tips & gratuity, mineral water, soft & hard drinks, porterage\r\n\r\n• Additional sightseeing or extra usage of vehicle, other than mentioned in the itinerary\r\n\r\n• Guide charges, Entry Fees & Camera Charges if any\r\n\r\n• VIP Darshan in Kamakhya Temple\r\n\r\n• Any cost arising due to natural calamities like cyclone, road blockage, political disturbances (strikes), etc (to be borne by the client and directly payable on the spot)\r\n\r\n• Any increase in taxes or fuel price, leading to increase in cost on surface transportation & land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure\r\n\r\n• Insurance\r\n\r\n• Anything that is not mentioned in Inclusions\r\n\r\n\r\n','The rates are valid till 24th November, 2022.\r\n','2022-12-25','2022-12-30',1,0,0,'2022-11-21 21:29:47','2022-11-21 21:29:47'),(201,541,349,2,1,0,61000,16000,'Amazing UAE','Dubai Tour Package','','Accomodation as per details mentioned above. \r\nTransfers from Dubai Airport to Howard Johnson Hotel – PVT\r\nTransfers from Howard Johnson to W Hotel Yas Island – PVT \r\nTransfers from W Hotel Yas Island to Lapita Resort Dubai – PVT \r\nTransfers from Lapita Resort to Dubai Airport – PVT \r\nEnroute Abu Dhabi City Tour \r\nLapita Stay with Park Access. \r\nYas Island Park Access\r\nDubai City Tour - SIC\r\nDesert Safari with BBQ Dinner - SIC\r\nMarina Harbour Dinner Cruise) - SIC\r\nDubai Dolphinarium - Dolphin & Seal Show (Regular Tickets) + PVT Transfers \r\nMiracle Garden – SIC \r\n','- Tourism Dirham is not included in above quotation and shall be directly payable by the guest.\r\nAnything not mentioned in Inclusions. ','','2022-12-13','2022-12-20',0,0,0,'2022-11-24 15:55:19','2022-11-24 16:33:55'),(202,537,13540,2,0,0,153000,25000,'North East Diaries','Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 01: Arrival-Guwahati\r\nUpon arrival meet and greet season, then drive to hotel. Check in Hotel. Evening leisure time .Stay at Guwahati.\r\n\r\nDay 02:Guwahati-Kaziranga (230 KM)\r\nWelcome to Awesome Assam. Meet and be assisted by our representative at the airport/Railway Station. Transfer to Kaziranga National Park, the home of the One Horn Indian Rhinoceros. Check in at your hotel/resort. Evening you may visit Orchid Park and the nearby Tea Plantations. Overnight stay at Kaziranga National Park. \r\n \r\nDay 03: Kaziranga National Park  - Shillong(270 KM) - 6 DEC\r\nEarly morning explore Kaziranga National Park on back of elephant(own cost). Apart from world\'s endangered One Horn Indian Rhinoceros, the Park sustains half the world\'s population of genetically pure Wild Water Buffaloes, over 1000 Wild elephants and perhaps the densest population of Royal Bengal Tiger anywhere. Kaziranga National Park is also a bird watcher\'s paradise and home to some 500 species of Birds. The Crested Serpent Eagle, Palla\'s Fishing Eagle, Greyheaded Fishing Eagle, Swamp Partridge, Bar-headed goose, whistling Teal, Bengal Florican, Storks, Herons and Pelicans are some of the species found here. We will return to the resort for breakfast. Proceed for a Jeep Safari.Stay at Kaziranga.\r\n\r\nDay 04: Kaziranga\r\nDay at Leisure\r\n\r\nDay 05: Kaziranga-Shillong (270 KM)\r\nDrive to Shillong, also called \'Scotland of the East\". Reach the majestic \r\nUmium Lake (Barapani). You may do the water sports here (Optional). On arrival at Shillong, check in at your hotel. Evening you can visit Police Bazaar which the biggest local market. Overnight stay in Shillong.  \r\n\r\nDay 06:  Shillong – Mawsynram – Mawphlang Sacred Forest – Shillong ( 60 KM) \r\nAfter breakfast visit Mawsynram which as per the new geological reports receives the highest rainfall in the world. The area is known for its many caves. Later visit Mawphlang Sacred Grove. It is one of the biggest Sacred Groves in Meghalaya.It is a well preserved forest by local community. Nothing can be taken out from the forest as this is being protected by the local deities.Visit Khasi model village.Stay at Shillong.\r\n\r\nDay 07: Shillong-Mawlynnong- Dawki (90 KM)\r\nAfter breakfast drive to visit Mawlynnong Village the cleanest village in India. This cute and colorful little village is known for its cleanliness.  It is situated 90 kms. from Cherrapunji and besides the picturesque village, offers many interesting sights such as the Living Root Bridge and another strange natural phenomenon of a boulder balancing on another rock. Stay at Dawki.\r\n\r\nDay 08: Dawki Local SS\r\nVisit Dawki, It is along the Indo-Bangladesh border. You can enjoy boating in the crystal clear waters of the Umgnot River.Evening leisure. Stay at Dawki.\r\n\r\nDay 09: Dawki- Krangsuri -Shillong (100 KM )\r\nMorning visit Indo-Bangladesh Border and then proceed to visit Krang Suri Falls. It is one of the best waterfalls in Meghalaya. You can also swim in a naturally formed pool here. You can also go behind the waterfall and see the water falling in front of you.Later drive to Shillong. Stay overnight in Shillong.\r\n\r\nDay 10: Shillong – Cherrapunji (65 KM)\r\nAfter breakfast drive to Cherrapunji, this is the wettest place in the world. Visit  Eco Park,  Nohkalikai Falls, Nohsngithiang Falls (Seven Sisters Falls), Mawsmai Cave,Arwah Cave.Return back to Shillong.Enroute visit Elephant Falls and Shillong Peak. Stay at  Cherrapunji.\r\n\r\nDay 11: Cherrapunji Double Decker Trekking ( 60 KM) \r\nWe proceed for a full day trekking to the Double Decker Living Root Bridge at Nongriat Village. We have to trek down 3200 steps approximately each way to the Double Decker Living Root Bridge. We can further trek down to the Rainbow Falls which take about 60 to 90 minutes from the Double Decker Living Root Bridge. (3400 Steps up and down).Stay at Cherrapunji.\r\n\r\nDay 12: Cherrapunji-Shillong(65 KM)\r\nVisit Wai Saodang and whistling village.Return to Shillong. Stay at Shillong.\r\n\r\nDay 13: Shillong-Guwahati\r\nToday after breakfast drive to Guwahati. Visit Kamakhya temple-one of the most prominent shakti pithas of India. If time permits enjoy a river cruise at river Brahmaputra(own cost).Stay at Guwahati.\r\n\r\nDay 14: Guwahati-Departure\r\nSay goodbye to North East. Tour concludes with memories.','','* Accommodation on double/Twin Sharing Basis\r\n* Pick up and drop off as per the itinerary from the respective Airport // Train Station\r\n* Daily Breakfast and Dinner\r\n* Elephant Safari at Kaziranga\r\n* 1 Round of Jeep Safari at Kaziranga National Park/Central or Western Range of the park.\r\n* Vehicle on point to point basis as per the itinerary.\r\n* Service of an Experience Driver for Entire Tour\r\n* Driver allowances, toll, parking, fuel etc.','* Personal Expenses such as Laundry, telephone, tips, gratuity, Food and drinks .\r\n* Any other food\r\n* Additional sightseeing or extra usage of vehicle, other than mentioned in the itinerary.\r\n* Camera fees, Guide / tour escort charges & Entrance Fees .\r\n* Elephant Safari at Kaziranga National Park.\r\n* Any cost arising due to natural calamities like, landslides, road blockage, political disturbances, etc (to be borne by the client, which is directly payable on the spot) .\r\n* Any increase in taxes or fuel price, leading to increase in cost on surface transportation & land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure .\r\n* Any other activity during the trip will be direct payment basis.\r\n* Insurance.\r\n* Air fare // Railway Tickets.\r\n* Anything which is not included in the inclusion // itinerary','The rates are valid till 30th November, 2022','2022-12-16','2022-12-29',0,0,0,'2022-11-27 12:02:28','2022-11-27 12:02:38'),(204,543,16002,4,0,0,54300,14000,'Amazing Bali','Full Day Tour with Benoa water sports including 1 x round of Banana boat, Parasailing / flying fish and Jet skii (parasailing subject to weather)  followed by Uluwatu sunset temple Tour with private transfers\r\n\r\nFull Day Denpasar City Tour followed Tanah Lot Temple Tour on Private basis (Visit Bajra Shandi Incl. entrance to 3D Interactive Art Museum), Bali Museum, Puputan Square ) with Hotel Inter Hotel Transfer by private transfers\r\n\r\nFull Day Kintamani tour with Ubud Village by private transfers\r\n','','Return Economy Class Airfare\r\n07 Nights Accommodation\r\nBB Basis\r\nMeet & Greet assistance at the airport \r\nReturn Airport & Inter Hotel transfer by Pvt Basis\r\nTransfers with air-conditioned vehicle\r\nEnglish speaking driver cum guide assistance\r\n','Compulsory dinner supplements incase of hotel surcharge\r\nAny surcharge at the hotel (Mini bar, Visiter fee ect.)\r\nPersonal insurance\r\nOther personal expenses\r\nSurcharge for peak season if any (Upon booking) \r\nExpenditure of a personal nature such as drinks, souvenirs and laundry\r\nAny cost not mentioned in the ‘Cost Includes’ section\"\r\nTCS 5%\r\n','','2023-04-01','2023-04-08',1,0,0,'2022-11-30 22:29:06','2022-11-30 22:29:06'),(205,545,16002,4,0,0,27200,6000,'Amazing Bali','Amazing Bali ','','Return Economy Class Airfare\r\nMeet & Greet assistance at the