 COMBI)\r\n* Night Safari Transfer (Return Transfers) - SIC 3 Adults + 01 Child (Ticket Only)\r\n\r\n2nd Day (1 Jun)\r\n* Half Day City Orientation Drive - SIC 3 Adults + 01 Child\r\n* Gardens By The Bay (Return Transfers) - SIC 3 Adults + 01 Child\r\n* Ticket (Cloud Forest + Flower Dome Ticket Only)\r\n\r\n3rd Day (2 Jun)\r\n* Universal Studios Transfer (Return Transfers) - SIC 3 Adults + 01 Child\r\n* Ticket Only (3 Adults + 01 Child)\r\n\r\n4th Day (3 Jun)\r\n* Full Day Sentosa Return Transfers- SIC 3 Adults + 01 Child\r\n* Sentosa Attractions Ticket (Combo 4 - Cable Car + Sea Aquarium + WOT)\r\n\r\n5th Day (4 Jun)\r\n* Singapore - Airport Departure Transfer (1 PRIVATE COMBI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* 4 Nights stay in 4 Star hotels mentioned above\r\n* Daily Breakfast\r\n* All sightseeing and transfers on Pvt/SIC as mentioned above\r\n* Travel Insurance\r\n* Visa Charges','* Any meal other than that mentioned above\r\n* Any type of personal expense like laundary, grooming, souvenir, etc.\r\n* Visa Courier Charges','The rates are valid till 27th April, 2023.','2023-05-31','2023-06-04',0,0,0,'2023-04-25 12:23:46','2023-04-25 12:30:40'),(279,675,117,7,1,0,0,0,'Africa Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n20th Sep: On arrival, meet and greet our representative at the JKIA Airport, short safari briefing and transfer to hotel for overnight stay. \r\n\r\n21st Sep: Breakfast and depart for Aberdare national park, approx 3-4 hrs drive. Arrive at the base hotel in time for lunch, after lunch transfer to the Ark lodge, enjoy an afternoon game drive or view wildlife from the hotel as animals drink from the water hole. \r\n\r\n22nd Sep:  After breakfast, check out and depart to Lake Elementaita, approx 4hrs drive. Lunch on arrival, afternoon at leisure , dinner and overnight stay. \r\n\r\n23rd Sep : Morning tea/coffee, check out and depart for the Masai Mara game reserve, approx 4-5 hrs drive. Enjoy lunch on arrival and later head out for an afternoon game drive at the park, dinner and overnight at the lodge. \r\n\r\n24th & 25th Sep:  Full day game drive at the Masai Mara, dinner and overnight at the park. \r\n\r\n26th Sep:  Breakfast, check out and depart for Nairobi, approx. 6hrs drive. On arrival, transfer to the JKIA Airport in time for your outbound flight. ','','Accommodation as stipulated in the itinerary or similar\r\nPrivate transportation in  4x4 Safari Land Cruiser with pop-up roof for easy game viewing & photography\r\nGame drives as indicated in the itinerary\r\nServices of experienced English-speaking driver-guides\r\nAll Government taxes, parks entrance fees and levies as per itinerary\r\nBottled drinking water while on safari \r\nTransfer to and from the Airport','Activities not mentioned above\r\nTravel & Personal accident insurance\r\nExcursions not detailed in above program\r\nTips & personal expenses such as telephone calls etc.\r\nVisas, travel/baggage insurance, laundry, beverages, tips\r\nOther item(s) not stated as included above','The rates are valid till 2nd May, 2023. Rooms are subject to availability. \r\n\r\n','2023-09-20','2023-09-26',0,0,0,'2023-04-26 00:43:04','2023-04-28 15:09:47'),(280,676,15500,6,1,0,1093000,130000,'Switzerland Diaries','7N Switzerland Stay in 3 star hotel with daily breakfast\r\n\r\nSuggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nFrom – To-Lucerne - Interlaken - Zermatt - Zurich or Geneva- Duration : 08 Days\r\n\r\nDay 1 : Swiss Border or Airport – Lucerne\r\n* Travel from any Swiss Border or Airport to the fabulous and quaint city of Lucerne. \r\n* Early afternoon proceed for an excursion to the famous dragon mountain, the Mt. Pilatus. \r\n* In the evening enjoy 1 hour Panoramic Yacht Cruise on Lake Lucerne (Saphir Cruise). \r\n* Overnight in Lucerne.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : Lucerne\r\n* Morning proceed to Engelberg and then for an excursion to Mt. Titlis including the Ice flyer c \r\n  chairlift. \r\n* Evening is free at leisure to explore the city on your own. \r\n* Overnight in Lucerne.\r\n\r\nDay 3 : Lucerne – Interlaken\r\n* Travel to Interlaken on the Interlaken-Lucerne Express. \r\n* Afternoon visit the Mt. Schilthorn to enjoy the panoramic view of the James Bond Mountain. You may \r\n  enjoy a coffee at the famous revolving restaurant (on own expense). \r\n* Overnight in Interlaken.\r\n\r\nDay 4 : Interlaken\r\n* Today morning walk down to the Interlaken Ost station for an exciting excursion of Jungfraujoch – \r\n  Top of Europe. It is one of the highest peaks in Europe, here you may spend the whole day with \r\n  different activities. \r\n* Overnight in Interlaken.\r\n\r\nDay 5 : Interlaken – Zermatt\r\n* Travel to Zermatt by train. \r\n* Rest of the day is free at leisure to explore this car free town by foot or by horse carriage. \r\n* Overnight in Zermatt.\r\n\r\nDay 6 : Zermatt\r\n* Take a trip to the Matterhorn Glacier Paradise. \r\n* Overnight in Zermatt.\r\n\r\nDay 7 : Zermatt – Zurich or Geneva\r\n* Travel by train from Zermatt to Zurich or Geneva. \r\n* The rest of the afternoon is free to explore the city on your own using the Swiss Pass or proceed \r\n  for an optional half day city tour. \r\n* Overnight in Zurich or Geneva\r\n\r\nDay 8 : Depart Zurich or Geneva\r\n* Depart Zurich or Geneva to any Swiss Border or Airport for your train or flight to the next destination.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nHotel Used : 3 Star\r\n\r\nLucerne:    Ambassador or Drei Konige or Similar; \r\nInterlaken: Chalet Swiss or Central Continental or Crystal or Similar; \r\nZermatt:    Adonis Hotel or Similar; \r\nZurich:     Hotel Bristol Zurich or Ibis Zurich City West or similar\r\nGeneva:     Hotel Kipling or Hotel Bernina Geneva or Similar\r\n','Cancellation policy will be advised at the time of booking. ','* 02 Nights Accommodation in Lucerne\r\n* 02 Nights Accommodation in Interlaken\r\n* 02 Nights Accommodation in Zermatt\r\n* 01 Night Accommodation in Zurich or Geneva\r\n* Daily Breakfast\r\n* Swiss Travel Pass (08 days – 02nd Class)\r\n* Travel Insurance\r\n','* Jungfraujoch – Top of Europe\r\n* Mt. Titlis incl iceflyer chairlift ride + glacier park\r\n* Mt. Pilatus\r\n* Matterhorn Glacier Paradise or Gornergrat\r\n* Mt. Schilthorn – Piz Gloria\r\n* Any meal other than that mentioned above\r\n* Any type of personal expense like laundary, grooming, souvenir, etc.\r\n* Visa Courier Charges\r\n','The rates are valid till 30th April, 2023. Rates are subject to change without prior notice and subject to availability. Rates are not valid during fair periods & blockout dates, when supplement costs will be applicable on the package. ','2023-06-18','2023-06-24',0,0,0,'2023-04-26 12:47:00','2023-04-26 15:48:36'),(281,677,6,1,0,0,12200,5000,'Delhi and Agra Diaries','Day 1: Delhi-Agra\r\nPick-up from the Hotel and drive to Agra and visit Taj Mahal and Red Fort.\r\nDrive back to in the evening.\r\n\r\nDay 3: Delhi-Gurugram \r\nPick-up from the Hotel and drive to TATTVA Wellness and Spa Center (Gurugram).\r\n\r\nSpa Details:\r\n\r\nDeep Tissue Massage\r\nDate:2023-05-01\r\nTime:12:00 PM-1:00 PM\r\nDuration:60','','* Honda Amaze or Hyundai Accent for all transfers and sightseeing.\r\n* Parking and Toll Charges\r\n* Massage Therapies','* Guide Charges\r\n* Any type of personal expenses.\r\n* Anything that is not mentioned in the Inclusions.','','2023-04-29','2023-05-01',0,0,0,'2023-04-26 18:16:26','2023-04-26 18:28:16'),(282,678,329,4,0,0,0,0,'Kuala Lumpur Diaries','04 Nights Stay – Kuala Lumpur – 01 June to 05 June 2023 ','','04 Nights Stay in KUL \r\nDaily Breakfast \r\nReturn Airport Transfers – PVT \r\nHalf Day Kul City Tour + KL Tower – SIC \r\nGenting Highland Tour + 02 Ways Cable Car + Batu Caves (Photo Stop) – SIC \r\nSunway Lagoon Theme Park + SIC Transfers \r\nTravel Insurance\r\nVisa Charges','* Any meal other than that mentioned above\r\n* Any type of personal expense like laundary, grooming, souvenir, etc.\r\n* TCS','The rates are valid till 30th April, 2023. The air fare is dynamic','2023-05-31','2023-06-05',1,0,0,'2023-04-27 18:18:28','2023-04-27 18:36:34'),(283,679,16002,4,0,0,0,0,'Bali-Indonesia','6 Nights Bali Stay with transfers and sightseeing.\r\nHotel: 5 nights In Grand Ixora/ 1 Night in Ayana Resort\r\n\r\nTentative Itinerary:\r\n \r\n15th June - Arrival\r\n16th June - Bali safari & Marine park with Jungle hopper on pvt\r\n17th June - Garuda Wisnu Kencana Cultural Park + Bird Park on pvt \r\n18th June - Kintamani  Tour with ubud on pvt\r\n19th June - Mengiat Beach +  Bali Hai Cruise on pvt \r\n20th June -  Full Day Tour Tanjung Glass bottom with Turtle Island with Tanah Lot on pvt basis\r\n21st June - Check out\r\n\r\n','','Delhi-Bali-Delhi Economy class airfare\r\n06 Nights Accommodation on BB Basis\r\n06 Dinners in an Indian Restaurant\r\nMeet & Greet assistance at the airport\r\nReturn Airport & Inter Hotel transfer by Pvt Basis\r\nTransfers with air-conditioned vehicle\r\nEnglish-speaking driver cum guide assistance\r\nTanah lot temple\r\nBali safari & Marine park with Jungle hopper\r\nFull Day Tour Tanjung Glass bottom with Turtle Island\r\nGaruda Wisnu Kencana Cultural Park\r\nBali Hai Cruise\r\nBird park \r\nKintamani with Ubud tour\r\nMengiat Beach\r\nTravel Insurance','Toll tax not included in the package cost - Mandara Toll Road to Nusa Dua\r\nAny meal other than the mentioned above\r\nAny surcharge at the hotel (Mini bar, Visiter fee ect.)\r\nOther personal expenses\r\nSurcharge for peak season if any (Upon booking) \r\nExpenditure of a personal nature such as drinks, souvenirs and laundry\r\nAny cost not mentioned in the ‘Cost Includes’ section\"\r\nTCS','The rates are valid till 15th April, 2023. Airfare is dynamic.','2023-06-15','2023-06-21',1,0,0,'2023-04-28 08:45:22','2023-04-28 08:45:22'),(284,682,15518,2,1,0,0,0,'Kerala Diaries ','5N/6D Kerala Stay in 3/4 star hotel with daily breakfast and dinner\r\n\r\nSuggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 (23 May 2023 - Tuesday) Cochin - Munnar(Arrival)\r\n\r\nMeet & Assist on arrival\r\nArrival Transfer - Cochin - Munnar(Arrival)\r\nOn arrival at the Cochin airport/railway station, meet our representative who will be there for your warm welcome and afterwards to transfer you to your already booked hotel in Munnar Proceed to Munnar. Visit Cheeyapara and Valara water falls on the way to Munnar. Through out the journey enjoy beautiful streams small waterfalls, Rubber, Pepper cardamom and Tea plantations and thick forests; God has blessed his own country with incomparable beauty on arrival at Munnar check in to Hotel.\r\n \r\nOvernight stay in Hotel/resort.\r\nThe Whispering Meadows (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\nAmuse Vista Resorts and Spa (Option 2) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 2 (24 May 2023 - Wednesday) Munnar Sightseeing \r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Amuse Vista Resorts and Spa/The Whispering Meadows\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed to enjoy full day sight seeing tour of Munnar. Rose Garden, Tea Garden, Photo Point, Madupetty Dam/Lake, Echo Point & Kundala Dam/Lake.\r\n \r\nOvernight stay in Hotel/resort.\r\nThe Whispering Meadows (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\nAmuse Vista Resorts and Spa (Option 2) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 3 (25 May 2023 - Thursday) Munnar - Thekkady\r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Amuse Vista Resorts and Spa/The Whispering Meadows\r\nTransfers - Munnar - Thekkady\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Thekkady .Thekkady is a world famous wildlife sanctuary and it is also called as Periyar. On arrival check in at Hotel. Afternoon visit wildlife sanctuary & enjoy the boating ( tickets charges are extra and subject to availability ). Visit spice plantations. Apart from being enjoyable these plantation tours gives tourists an insight into the growing, harvesting and processing of spices. Evening will be free for Cultural show ( Kathakali & Kalaripayattu on direct payment ) & local shopping.Overnight stay at Thekkady.\r\n\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel \r\nPeriyar Meadows Leisure Hotels (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\nSpicegrove (Option 2) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 4 (26 May 2023 - Friday) Thekkady to Alleppey\r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Spicegrove/Periyar Meadows Leisure Hotels\r\nTransfers - Thekkady to Alleppey\r\nMorning after breakfast leave for Alleppey, Allappuza famous for its backwaters. Visit Alleppey beach, sunset and enjoy shopping if staying in Alleppey. Visit Alleppey Beach and Backwaters. Enjoy all the amenities of this hotel/resort for a day which includes fishing in the backwaters (depends on the hotel/resort selected) Overnight stay at same hotel/resort\"\r\n\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel \r\nPagoda Resort (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\nOxygen Resort Alleppey (Option 2) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 5 (27 May 2023 - Saturday) Alleppey Day 02\r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Oxygen Resort Alleppey/Pagoda Resort\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Alleppey Day 02\r\nAfter Breakfast Proceed to Sight seeing in Alleppey.Visit Crystal Museum, Alleppey Beach and Jain Temple. Overnight stay at Alleppey.\r\n\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel\r\nPagoda Resort (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\nOxygen Resort Alleppey (Option 2) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 6 (28 May 2023 - Sunday) Alleppey -Cochin departure transfer\r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Oxygen Resort Alleppey/Pagoda Resort\r\nDeparture Transfer - Alleppey -Cochin departure transfer\r\nAfter breakfast check out from the hotel and Transferred to Cochin Airport / Railway station for the for the departure.\r\n\r\n','','* Delhi-Cochin-Delhi Economy Class airfare\r\n* 5 Nights stay in 3/4 Star hotels/resorts mentioned above\r\n* Daily Breakfast and Dinner\r\n* All sightseeings and transfers\r\n* All Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\n* All Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost\r\n\r\n','* Any meal other than that mentioned above\r\n* Any type of personal expense like laundary, grooming, souvenir, etc.\r\n* Entry Fees To Monuments And Palaces\r\n* Any Cost Arising Due To Natural Calamities Like Landslides, Roadblocks, Etc\r\n* Only Non Ac Rooms Are Provided In Munnar And Thekkady As They Are Hill Stations\r\n* Any Increase In Taxes Or Fuel Leading To An Increase In Surface Transport\r\n\r\n','The rates are valid till 7th May, 2023. The air fare is dynamic','2023-05-23','2023-05-28',1,0,0,'2023-05-04 12:30:13','2023-05-04 18:44:04'),(285,683,126,4,0,0,19400,17600,'Jaipur and Agra Diaries','1N Jaipur - 1N Agra\r\n\r\nDay 1: bangalore -Jaipur\r\nPick-up from the airport. Check-in at the hotel and Explore historical places like Amer Fort, Hawa Mahal, Jal Mahal and Jantar-Mantar. Overnight stay at the hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 2: Jaipur-Agra\r\nAfter breakfast, check-out from the hotel and drive to Agra. Check-in at the hotel and visit Taj Mahal, Red Fort and Fatehpur Sikri. Overnight stay at the hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 3: After breakfast, check-out from the hotel and drive to airport. Trip ends here with beautiful memories.','','* Hotel accommodation at Jaipur and Agra.\r\n* Daily breakfast and Lunch/Dinner\r\n* Innova Crysta for all transfers and sightseeing.\r\n* Parking and Toll Charges','* Guide Charges\r\n* Any other meal other than mentioned above.\r\n* Any type of personal expenses.\r\n* Anything that is not mentioned in the Inclusions.','The airfare is dynamic and subject to change.','2023-05-24','2023-05-26',1,0,0,'2023-05-04 19:09:39','2023-05-04 19:23:51'),(286,684,281,4,0,0,32000,18000,'Jaipur, Ranthambore and Agra Diaries','1N Agra- 1N Ranthambore - 1N Jaipur\r\n\r\nDay 1: bangalore -Agra\r\nPick-up from the airport. Explore historical places like Taj Mahal and Red Fort. Check-in at the hotel  and Overnight stay at the hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 2: Agra-Ranthambore\r\nAfter breakfast, check-out from the hotel and drive to Ranthambore. Check-in at the hotel and Going for Open Jeep Safari. Overnight stay at the hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 3: Ranthambore-Jaipur\r\nAfter breakfast, check-out from the hotel and drive to Jaipur and Explore historical places like Amer Fort, Hawa Mahal, Jal Mahal and Jantar-Mantar and After Exploring drive to airport. Trip ends here with beautiful memories.','','* Hotel accommodation at Ranthambore and Agra.\r\n* Daily breakfast and Lunch/Dinner\r\n* Innova Crysta for all transfers and sightseeing.\r\n* Parking and Toll Charges\r\n* Safari Charges','* Guide Charges\r\n* Any other meal other than mentioned above.\r\n* Any type of personal expenses.\r\n* Anything that is not mentioned in the Inclusions.','The airfare is dynamic and subject to change and guide and monuments tickets will be directly purchased from respective monuments.','2023-05-24','2023-05-26',1,0,0,'2023-05-05 16:19:11','2023-05-05 16:43:52'),(287,686,281,4,0,0,42500,23400,'Jaipur, Ranthambore and Agra Diaries','1N Agra- 1N Ranthambore - 1N Jaipur\r\n\r\nDay 1: bangalore -Agra\r\nPick-up from the airport. Explore historical places like Taj Mahal and Red Fort. Check-in at the hotel  and Overnight stay at the hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 2: Agra-Ranthambore\r\nAfter breakfast, check-out from the hotel and drive to Ranthambore. Check-in at the hotel and Going for Open Private Jeep Safari. Overnight stay at the hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 3: Ranthambore-Jaipur\r\nAfter breakfast, check-out from the hotel and drive to Jaipur and Explore historical places like Amer Fort, Hawa Mahal, Jal Mahal and Jantar-Mantar and After Exploring drive to airport. Trip ends here with beautiful memories.','','* Hotel accommodation at Ranthambore and Agra.\r\n* Daily breakfast and Lunch/Dinner\r\n* Innova Crysta for all transfers and sightseeing.\r\n* Parking and Toll Charges\r\n* Safari Charges','* Guide Charges\r\n* Any other meal other than mentioned above.\r\n* Any type of personal expenses.\r\n* Anything that is not mentioned in the Inclusions.','The airfare is dynamic and subject to change and guide and monuments tickets will be directly purchased from respective monuments.','2023-05-24','2023-05-26',1,0,0,'2023-05-06 18:28:03','2023-05-22 13:51:37'),(288,687,15518,2,1,0,0,0,'Kerala Diaries ','5N/6D Kerala Stay in 3/4 star hotel with daily breakfast and dinner\r\n\r\nSuggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 1 (23 May 2023 - Tuesday) Cochin Arrival\r\n\r\nMeet & Assist on arrival\r\nArrival Transfer - Cochin Arrival\r\n\r\nArrival at Cochin and transfer to hotel. Check in at Hotel. In Cochin Visit the Dutch Palace-built by the Portuguese in 1557 and subsequently renovated by the Dutch after 1663. The murals are perhaps the best in India. Jewish Synagogue - built in 1568 and the oldest Synagogue in the Commonwealth are at Mattancherry. St. Francis Church - built in 1510 and the oldest European church in India, Chinese Fishing Nets- introduced by the court of Kublai Khan can be seen in Fort Cochin. Fort Cochin Beach etc. Overnight stay at Cochin\r\n\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel\r\nBroad Bean Hotel (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\nStarlit Suites Kochi (Option 2) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nDay 2 (24 May 2023 - Wednesday) Cochin - Thekkady\r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Starlit Suites Kochi/Broad Bean Hotel\r\nTransfers - Cochin - Thekkady\r\n\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Thekkady .Thekkady is a world famous wildlife sanctuary and it is also called as Periyar. On arrival check in at Hotel. Afternoon visit wildlife sanctuary & enjoy the boating ( tickets charges are extra and subject to availability ). Visit spice plantations. Apart from being enjoyable these plantation tours gives tourists an insight into the growing, harvesting and processing of spices. Evening will be free for Cultural show ( Kathakali & Kalaripayattu on direct payment ) & local shopping.Overnight stay at Thekkady.\r\n\r\n\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel \r\nPeriyar Meadows Leisure Hotels (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\nSpicegrove (Option 2) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 3 (25 May 2023 - Thursday) Thekkady to Alleppey\r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Spicegrove/Periyar Meadows Leisure Hotels\r\nTransfers - Thekkady to Alleppey\r\n\r\nMorning after breakfast leave for Alleppey, Allappuza famous for its backwaters. Visit Alleppey beach, sunset and enjoy shopping if staying in Alleppey. Visit Alleppey Beach and Backwaters. Enjoy all the amenities of this hotel/resort for a day which includes fishing in the backwaters (depends on the hotel/resort selected) Overnight stay at same hotel/resort\"\r\n\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel \r\nOxygen Resort Alleppey (Option 2) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\nPagoda Resort (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 4 (26 May 2023 - Friday) Alleppey to Kovalam\r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Pagoda Resort/Oxygen Resort Alleppey\r\nTransfers - Alleppey to Kovalam\r\n\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel Houseboat and transfer to Kovalam. Check in at Hotel. Kovalam is an evergreen and pleasant climatic beach. Kovalam is a dreamland for tourists all over the world. With high rock promontory and a calm bay of blue waters, this beach paradise creates a unique aquarelle on moonlit nights. Kovalam was brought to the public eye by the Maharaja of Travancore. Over the past three decades, the place has been well developed, and now figures prominently on the world tourism map. Overnight stay at Kovalam.\r\n\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel \r\nAadisaktthi Ayurveda Leisure Village Resort, (Option 2) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\nJasmine Palace (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 5 (27 May 2023 - Saturday) Kovalam – Thiruvananthapuram – Kovalam\r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Aadisaktthi Ayurveda Leisure Village Resort,/Jasmine Palace\r\n\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed for Sightseeing. Visit Padmanabha Swami Temple, Kuthiramalika Palace Museum, Zoo, Napier  Museum & Veli Tourist Village. Overnight stay at Kovalam.\r\n\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel \r\nAadisaktthi Ayurveda Leisure Village Resort, (Option 2) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\nJasmine Palace (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 6 (28 May 2023 - Sunday) Kovalam to Thiruvananthapuram Drop\r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Aadisaktthi Ayurveda Leisure Village Resort,/Jasmine Palace\r\n\r\nDeparture Transfer - Kovalam to Thiruvananthapuram Drop\r\nMorning after breakfast check out the Hotel and drive towards the Thiruvananthapuram Airport/Railway station for your onward journey. Tour ends with happy memories.','','* Delhi-Cochin and Thiruvananthapuram-Delhi Economy Class airfare\r\n* 5 Nights stay in 3/4 Star hotels/resorts mentioned above\r\n* Daily Breakfast and Dinner\r\n* All sightseeings and transfers\r\n* All Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\n* All Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost\r\n\r\n','* Any meal other than that mentioned above\r\n* Any type of personal expense like laundary, grooming, souvenir, etc.\r\n* Entry Fees To Monuments And Palaces\r\n* Any Cost Arising Due To Natural Calamities Like Landslides, Roadblocks, Etc\r\n* Only Non Ac Rooms Are Provided In Thekkady As They Are Hill Stations\r\n* Any Increase In Taxes Or Fuel Leading To An Increase In Surface Transport\r\n\r\n','The airfare is dynamic and subject to change. ','2023-05-23','2023-05-28',1,0,0,'2023-05-08 10:52:20','2023-05-08 17:19:13'),(289,691,4818,2,0,0,0,0,'Bhutan Diaries','7N/8D Bhutan Stay in hotel with daily breakfast and dinner\r\n\r\nSuggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n1st Day - (Friday 23rd June) : NJP Railway Station/IXB Airport to Phuentsholing - Pick up \r\nApprox Distance: 157 Km • Est. Travel Time: 5 hours \r\nMeet & Greet on arrival at NJP Railway Station / IXB Airport and transfer to Phuentsholing (961 ft.) - The Gateway of Bhutan by Road from India. It is a thriving commercial centre on the northern edge of the Indian Plains. On arrival check in at the hotel. In the evening, you may choose to relax at the hotel or walk around the Phuentsholing town. Overnight stay at Phuentsholing.\r\n\r\n2nd Day - (Saturday 24th June) : Phuentsholing to Thimphu - Transfer \r\nApprox Distance: 150 Km • Est. Travel Time: 5 hours \r\nAfter breakfast, complete the immigration formalities and transfer to Thimphu (7,710 ft.) the capital city of Bhutan. On the way, stop at places to view scenery and for Photography. On arrival check in at the hotel. In the evening, you may choose to relax at the hotel or take a leisure walk around the Thimphu City. Overnight stay at Thimphu.\r\n\r\n3rd Day - (Sunday 25th June) : Thimphu - Sightseeing \r\nAfter breakfast, visit Kuenselphodrang (Buddha Dordenma) for a panoramic view of Thimphu valley and see the largest Buddha statue in Bhutan. Then, visit the National Memorial Chorten and Folk Heritage Museum. In the afternoon, visit Sangaygang View Point for a stunning view of Thimphu, Takin Preserve Centre to see the national animal of Bhutan, and Changangkha Lhakhang, a popular Buddhist temple. In the evening, visit Tashichho Dzong, the seat of the National Government and Central Monastic Body. Overnight stay in Thimphu.\r\n\r\n4th Day - (Monday 26th June) : Thimphu to Punakha/Wangdue - Transfer and Sightseeing \r\nApprox Distance: 78 Km • Est. Travel Time: 3 hours \r\nAfter breakfast, drive to Punakha/Wangdue and stop at Dochu-La-Pass to view the Himalayas and the 108 Druk Wangyel Chortens. Check in at the hotel upon arrival and visit Punakha Dzong, the former seat of the Government and winter residence of Je-Khenpo. Take a short hike to visit Chhimi Lhakhang, also known as “The Temple of Fertility”. Evening free for leisure. Overnight stay in Punakha/Wangdue.\r\n\r\n5th Day - (Tuesday 27th June) : Punakha/Wangdue to Paro - Transfer and Sightseeing \r\nApprox Distance: 125 Km • Est. Travel Time: 5 hours \r\nAfter breakfast drive to Paro (7,483 ft.). On the way stop at Lamperi to visit Royal Botanical Park. This park is a treat for nature lovers as the 36 species of exotic rhododendron and approximately 220 types of charming birds will make your day unforgettable. On arrival check in at the hotel. Afternoon visit Ta Dzong - National Museum with an excellent collection of arts, relics, religious thangkha, etc. Then visit the Rinpung Dzong - Meaning \"fortress of the heap of jewels\". The dzong now serves as the administrative and judicial seat of Paro. Rest of the evening at leisure. Overnight stay at Paro\r\n\r\n6th Day - (Wednesday 28th June) : Paro - Taktshang Monastery Excursion \r\nApprox Distance: 40 Km • Est. Travel Time: 1 hour 30 minutes \r\nAfter breakfast, drive to Taktshang Monastery and hike uphill for 2-3 hours to reach the primary Lhakhang built surrounding Guru Rinpoche’s meditation cave. Legend has it that Guru Rinpoche flew here on the back of a tigress, giving the monastery its name “Tiger’s Nest”. In the afternoon, visit Drukgyel Dzong to explore the ramparts and enjoy the view of Mt. Jhomolhari, and then visit Kichu Lhakhang, one of the oldest temples in Bhutan. Overnight stay in Paro\r\n\r\n7th Day - (Thursday 29th June) : Paro to Phuentsholing - Transfer \r\nApprox Distance: 145 Km • Est. Travel Time: 5 hours \r\nAfter breakfast check out from hotel and transfer to Phuentsholing. On arrival check in at the hotel. In the evening, you may choose to relax at the hotel or walk around the Phuentsholing town. Overnight stay at Phuentsholing.\r\n \r\n8th Day - (Friday 30th June) : Phuentsholing to NJP Railway Station/IXB Airport - Drop \r\nApprox Distance: 170 Km • Est. Travel Time: 5 hours \r\nAfter breakfast check out from the hotel and drive to NJP Railway Station / IXB Airport for your onward journey.','','* 7 Nights stay in hotel mentioned above\r\n* Daily Breakfast and Dinner\r\n* All sightseeing and transfers on Pvt/SIC as mentioned above\r\n* Exclusive Non-a/c vehicle for all transfers & sightseeing as per itinerary. \r\n* Guide / Escort charges. \r\n* Accommodation on double/twin sharing basis. All the rooms are base category, if not mentioned otherwise ','* Personal expenses such as laundry, telephone bills, bar bills, tips & gratuity, bottled water and cost for \r\n  other activities such as rafting, rock climbing, paragliding, porterage, etc. \r\n* Additional sightseeing or extra usage of vehicle, other than mentioned in the itinerary. \r\n* Entrance Fees for museums and monuments. \r\n* Any meal other than that mentioned above\r\n','The airfare is dynamic and subject to change.','2023-06-23','2023-06-30',1,0,0,'2023-05-12 13:46:09','2023-05-13 17:06:48'),(290,692,15535,2,0,0,89000,24000,'Wonderful Tour of Ladakh','7N Ladakh Stay in hotel with daily breakfast and dinner\r\n\r\nSuggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDAY 01: ARRIVE LEH  \r\nArrival Leh by morning flight and transfer to the hotel. After welcome drink take a complete rest for acclimatization to the height altitude of Leh (3500 meters). In the late afternoon drive to the city for an orientation walk in the markets‚ followed by a visit to Shanti Stupa‚ Leh palace. Dinner and overnight in hotel. \r\n\r\nDAY 02: LEH TO SHAM VALLEY (75 KMS / 4 HRS)  \r\nAfter breakfast you drive downstream along the River Indus on Leh – Kargil Highway. Enroute visiting Gurudwara Patthar Sahib Nestled deep in the Himalayas, A drive of another 4 km took us to Magnetic Hill which defies the law of gravity & further Driving through a picturesque landscape we reached the Confluence Of The Indus And Zanskar River, Just before Saspul a road to the right takes you for your visit to the Likir Monastery, Likir is one of the most active monasteries in the region. As you drive up to the monastery a recently installed colossal gilded image of the Maitreya out in the open is one of the most impressive sights in Ladakh. After visiting the Monastery, you continue your drive along the River Indus to Tingmosgang en route visiting Ridzong Monastery, there is the option to walk up to the Monastery for those that wish to do so. Hidden at the end of a steep valley, the first view of the Monastery is dramatic. After visiting above places we drive further and check in at our camp / hotel for overnight stay. \r\n\r\nDAY 03: SHAM VALLEY TO LEH VIA LAMAYURU (180 KMS / 05 – 06 HRS)  \r\nPost breakfast you drive to the 11th Century Lamayuru Monastery en route visiting the mesmerizing Moon Landscapes (you will believe why the name of this area is Moonland. Exactly the same formations of Land are visible as on the moon), Lamayuru is spectacularly located along the valley plain and surrounded by mountains on all sides. On your return drive to Leh you first visit the Alchi Gompa. The complex of temples located within the village is the most celebrated of Ladakh’s monasteries and dates back to the 11th century. After visiting Alchi we drive back to Leh. Finally, you arrive back at Leh for an overnight stay at your Hotel. \r\n \r\nDAY 04: LEH–NUBRA VALLEY VIA KHARDUNG LA 18,390 FT. (120 KMS / 4 – 5 HRS)  \r\nPost breakfast we drive to Nubra Valley. The road journey from Leh to Nubra Valley passes over Khardung La (The Highest Motorable Road In The World) at 5,602 Mtrs / 18,390 Ft, around 39 km from Leh. From the pass, one can see all the way south over the Indus valley to seemingly endless peaks and ridges of the Zanskar range, and north to the giants of the Saser massif. Nubra Valley is popularly known as Ldumra or the valley of flowers. It is situated in the north of Ladakh between the Karakoram and Ladakh ranges of the Himalayas. The average altitude of the valley is 10,000 Ft. above sea level. Upon arrival in Nubra we check in at our Camp / Hotel in Hunder for Overnight stay. In the evening you can walk around the tiny villages to see how the locals live in this part of the world. Overnight Stay at the Camp or Hotel \r\n \r\nDAY 05: IN NUBRA (HUNDER VILLAGE) –EXCURSION TO TURTUK \r\nAfter an early breakfast, proceed to Turtuk (A village that was won by India in the 1971 war with Pakistan) and extremely close to the border. Visit a 16th Century Mosque, (comprising of a touch of Turkish & Iranian culture), ruined fort of Dhards and Monastery. Admire the magnificent view of the famous K2 peak (The second highest peak in the world after Mount Everest). Later back to hotel for overnight stay. \r\n\r\nDAY 06: NUBRA VALLEY TO PANGONG LAKE (150 KMS / 5 HRS) \r\nDrive to Hunder after breakfast, ride a bacterian camel in the sand dunes and stop at Diskit for some shopping. Later, take a tough yet scenic drive via Agham & Shyok Valley to reach Pangong Tso passing through Changthang villages. Enjoy the sudden view of the lake at 14,000 feet upon arrival and check in at Camp/Hotel. Dinner and overnight stay at the hotel.\r\n \r\nDAY 07: PANGONG LAKE TO LEH VIA CHANGLA (140 KMS / 6 HRS) \r\nMorning at leisure to explore the beauty of lake and later we drive back to Leh via Changla Pass 5486 Mtrs en route visiting Hemis Gompa, the largest monastic foundation of Drukpa Kagyu Order of Tibetan Buddhism. And futher to Thiksey an impressive complex rising tier upon tier on a hill above the village and another 5 Kms driving through a picturesque landscape we reach to Shey Palace, The ancient capital of Ladakh & 3 Idiots Rancho School. Drive further to Leh. Dinner & Overnight at Hotel. \r\n \r\nDAY 08: DEPART LEH (FLY OUT) \r\nTour concludes. Through a punctual transfer to the Domestic Airport to catch the flight for your onward destination. \r\n\r\nTour Ends But Sweet Memories Remains Always','','* Delhi-Leh-Delhi Economy class airfare\r\n* Accommodation in Deluxe room on Double/twin sharing.\r\n* Assistance upon arrival at Leh Hotel  \r\n* Traditional welcome in the Hotel with Welcome Drink (Hot Tea / Coffee / Kahwa) on arrival  \r\n* 07 Nights Accommodation twin/double sharing basis as per the Itinerary \r\n* Meal Plan - 07 Breakfast & 07 Dinner \r\n* Return airport and round-trip transfers along with all sightseeing tours by Non-Ac Innova \r\n* Wild Life fees & Red Cross fee \r\n* All toll taxes/Parking fee/Driver allowance \r\n* Ladakh Entry Fee  \r\n* Ecological development fee  \r\n\r\n\r\n','* Personal expenses such as laundry, telephone bills, bar bills, tips & gratuity, bottled water and cost for\r\n  other activities such as rafting, rock climbing, paragliding, porterage, etc.\r\n* Additional sightseeing or extra usage of vehicle, other than mentioned in the itinerary.\r\n* Any meal other than that mentioned above','The airfare is dynamic and subject to change. The rates are valid till 16th May, 2023.','2023-06-23','2023-06-30',1,0,0,'2023-05-12 16:01:41','2023-05-12 23:17:33'),(291,693,15518,2,0,0,0,0,'Kerala Diaries ','7N/8D Kerala Stay in hotel with daily breakfast and dinner\r\n\r\nSuggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 (23 Jun 2023 - Friday) Cochin Arrival\r\nMeet & Assist on arrival\r\nArrival Transfer - Cochin Arrival\r\n\r\nArrival at Cochin and transfer to hotel. Check in at Hotel. In Cochin Visit the Dutch Palace-built by the Portuguese in 1557 and subsequently renovated by the Dutch after 1663. The murals are perhaps the best in India. Jewish Synagogue - built in 1568 and the oldest Synagogue in the Commonwealth are at Mattancherry. St. Francis Church - built in 1510 and the oldest European church in India, Chinese Fishing Nets- introduced by the court of Kublai Khan can be seen in Fort Cochin. Fort Cochin Beach etc. Overnight stay at Cochin\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Broad Bean Hotel (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 2 (24 Jun 2023 - Saturday) Cochin to Munnar\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Gokulam Park\r\nTransfers - Cochin to Munnar\r\n\r\n\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Munnar. Munnar is 1800 mts above sea level and also the place of South India\'s highest peak (Anamudi - 2695 mts). On the way visit Valara, Cheeyappara waterfalls & Tea Plantations. Check in to Hotel. Afternoon visit Rajamala (Eravikulam National Park - open as per the directions by the forest authorities ), the best place to see Nilgiri Tahr (Hermitragus Hilarious) - the mountain goat of South India & Tea Museum.  Evening have a short visit at Munnar town. You can see the beautiful tea estates like a green paradise. Overnight stay at Munnar.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Misty Lake Resort (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 3 (25 Jun 2023 - Sunday) Munnar Sightseeing DAY 02\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Misty Lake Resort/Trivers Resort\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Munnar Sightseeing DAY 02\r\n\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed to enjoy full day sight seeing tour of Munnar. Rose Garden, Tea Garden, Photo Point, Madupetty Dam/Lake, Echo Point & Kundala Dam/Lake. \r\n\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Misty Lake Resort (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 4 (26 Jun 2023 - Monday) Munnar - Thekkady\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Trivers Resort\r\nTransfers - Munnar - Thekkady\r\n\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Thekkady .Thekkady is a world famous wildlife sanctuary and it is also called as Periyar. On arrival check in at Hotel. Afternoon visit wildlife sanctuary & enjoy the boating ( tickets charges are extra and subject to availability ). Visit spice plantations. Apart from being enjoyable these plantation tours gives tourists an insight into the growing, harvesting and processing of spices. Evening will be free for Cultural show ( Kathakali & Kalaripayattu on direct payment ) & local shopping. Overnight stay at Thekkady.\r\n\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Periyar Meadows Leisure Hotels (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 5 (27 Jun 2023 - Tuesday) Thekkady to Alleppey\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Periyar Meadows Leisure Hotels\r\nTransfers - Thekkady to Alleppey\r\n\r\nMorning after breakfast leave for Alleppey, Allappuza famous for its backwaters. Visit Alleppey beach, sunset and enjoy shopping if staying in Alleppey. Visit Alleppey Beach and Backwaters. Enjoy all the amenities of this hotel/resort for a day which includes fishing in the backwaters (depends on the hotel/resort selected) Overnight stay at same hotel/resort\"\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Pagoda Resort (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 6 (28 Jun 2023 - Wednesday) Alleppey to Kovalam\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Punnamada Backwater Resort\r\nTransfers - Alleppey to Kovalam\r\n\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel Houseboat and transfer to Kovalam. Check in at Hotel. Kovalam is an evergreen and pleasant climatic beach. Kovalam is a dreamland for tourists all over the world. With high rock promontory and a calm bay of blue waters, this beach paradise creates a unique aquarelle on moonlit nights. Kovalam was brought to the public eye by the Maharaja of Travancore. Over the past three decades, the place has been well developed, and now figures prominently on the world tourism map. Overnight stay at Kovalam.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Jasmine Palace (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 7 (29 Jun 2023 - Thursday) Kovalam – Trivandrum – Kovalam\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Jasmine Palace\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Kovalam – Trivandrum – Kovalam\r\n\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed for Sightseeing. Visit Padmanabha Swami Temple, Kuthiramalika Palace Museum, Zoo, Napier  Museum & Veli Tourist Village. Overnight stay at Kovalam.\r\n\r\nOvernight Stay at Jasmine Palace (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 8 (30 Jun 2023 - Friday) Kovalam to Trivandrum Drop\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Jasmine Palace\r\nDeparture Transfer - Kovalam to Trivandrum Drop\r\n\r\nMorning after breakfast check out the Hotel and drive towards the Trivandrum Airport/Railway station for your onward journey. Tour ends with happy memories.','','* Delhi-Cochin and Thiruvananthapuram-Delhi Economy Class airfare\r\n* 7 Nights stay in hotels/resorts mentioned above\r\n* Daily Breakfast and Dinner\r\n* All sightseeings and transfers\r\n* All Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\n* All Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost\r\n* Accommodation on Twin Sharing Basis','* Any meal other than that mentioned above\r\n* Any type of personal expense like laundary, grooming, souvenir, etc.\r\n* Only Non Ac Rooms Are Provided In Thekkady As They Are Hill Stations','The airfare is dynamic and subject to change.','2023-06-23','2023-06-30',1,0,0,'2023-05-13 15:03:11','2023-05-13 15:03:11'),(292,694,14820,3,0,0,462700,80000,'Norway-Iceland-Denmark','4N Norway - 4N Iceland - 4N Denmark','','Inclusion:-\r\n# Flights\r\n# Accommodation\r\n# Daily Breakfast\r\n# Oslo- Transfer from Airport to Hotel on PVT\r\n# 24hrs City Sightseeing Oslo Hop-On Hop-Off Tour\r\n# The original Norway, in a nutshell, 08:25 Oslo- MYRDAL- FLÅM- GUDVANGEN- VOSS- BERGEN 20:40\r\n# Oslo- Transfer from Hotel to Airport on PVT\r\n# Reykjavik - Transfer from Airport to Hotel on PVT\r\n# Golden Circle Classic Day Trip from Reykjavik (10:00 with Pick up at 09:30 10:00), Reykjavik\r\n# Northern Lights Premium Tour From Reykjavik (Pickup at designated locations 21:30)\r\n# Reykjavik - Transfer from Hotel to Airport on PVT\r\n# Copenhagen - Transfer from Airport to Hotel/Accommodation on PVT\r\n# Copenhagen - Transfer from Hotel/Accommodation to Airport on PVT\r\n# Visa Charges\r\n# Travel Insurance\r\n\r\n\r\n# 24-Hour Bergen Hop-On Hop-Off Sightseeing Tour\r\n\r\n\r\n','','','2023-09-03','2023-09-15',1,0,0,'2023-05-15 11:32:14','2023-05-15 11:33:10'),(293,695,16002,2,0,0,0,0,'Bali Diaries','6 Nights Bali Stay with transfers and sightseeing.\r\n\r\nSuggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 (05 Jul 2023 - Wednesday)\r\nTransfer in to Select Hotel 	 \r\nPick up from Airport and drop to Hotel \r\n\r\nDay 2 (06 Jul 2023 - Thrusday)\r\nTanjung Benoa Water Sports + Uluwatu Tour\r\nwater creation center (carry 1 pair of cloth with you)	 \r\n1 Round Banana Boat	 \r\n[other activities on your own account]	 \r\nUluwatu Temple\r\n\r\nDay 3 (07 Jul 2023 - Friday)\r\nBreakfast at the hotel. Pick up early morning at hotel for Nusa Penida West Island Tour with\r\n06.30 AM : Driver pick up time from your hotel (depending of the hotel location)	 \r\nVisit -Crystal bay, Broken beach ,Angel billabong, Lunch at Local Restaurant.	 \r\nKelingkinhg Kliff, Kelingkinhg Kliff Selfie, \r\n\r\nDay 4 (08 Jul 2023 - Saturday)\r\nBedugul + Tanah lot tour	\r\nBedugul - ulun danu temple at britain lake 	 \r\nTanha lot temple \r\n\r\nDay 5 (09 Jul 2023 - Sunday)\r\nInter Hotel Transfer + Kintamani + Ubud Tour	\r\nFull Day Tour Visit:Mas/Celuk for local art & craft market	 \r\ncontinue visit Kintmani mount batur volcano, Spices Garden and Ubud Market	 \r\nTegalalang rice terrace 	 \r\n 	 \r\nDay 6 (10 Jul 2023 - Monday)\r\nDay at leisure \r\n\r\nDay 7 (11 Jul 2023 - Tuesday)\r\nTransfer Out','','* Delhi-Bali-Delhi Economy class airfare	\r\n* All Transfer on private basis\r\n* Travel Insurance\r\n* Inter hotel transfer on private basis\r\n* Daily Breakfast \r\n* One Lunch at Local Restaurant','* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Any surcharge at the hotel (Mini bar, \r\n  Visiter fee ect.)\r\n* Other personal expenses\r\n* Surcharge for peak season if any (Upon \r\n  booking)\r\n* Expenditure of a personal nature such as \r\n  drinks, souvenirs and laundry\r\n* TCS','The airfare is dynamic and subject to change.','2023-07-04','2023-07-11',1,0,0,'2023-05-17 17:09:48','2023-05-17 19:11:31'),(294,696,2841,2,0,0,0,0,'Port Blair Diaries','5 Nights / 6 Days | 3 Nights Port Blair/ 2 Nights Havelock Island\r\n\r\nSuggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1: Arrival – Port Blair – Cellular Jail - Light & Sound Show\r\nPort Blair\r\n* Arrival, Meet-Greet with our airport representative and Transfer to your booked hotel/ resort\r\n* Evening, visit to historic Cellular Jail followed by Light & Sound Show\r\n* Please note, we will drop guest at parking area near jail and guest must walk around 200 metre\r\nand return after completion of L&S show.\r\n* Guest has to come out after visiting jail and re-enter for L&S show, Guests can walk around the bay side in free time.\r\n* L&S show timing is in between 1800 Hrs- 1900hrs subject to availability\r\n* The free time between jail visit & L&S show can be utilised in self-exploration of illuminated Marina Park and Sea shore area, evenings are pleasant and happening here.\r\n\r\nDay 2: Port Blair- Havelock- Radha Nagar Beach\r\nHavelock Island\r\n* Pick up from hotel to Port Blair Jetty for your onward journey to Havelock\r\n* If you have morning ferry, ask hotel to provide Packed breakfast (Subject to hotel policy)\r\n* Arrival, Meet- Greet by our local representative and transfer to your booked hotel/ Resort\r\n* Afternoon, Visit to Blue Flag certified “Radha Nagar Beach” for swim and relaxation.\r\n* Do not forget to carry changing cloths and towel\r\n* It’s not permitted to board vehicle with wet cloths, please cooperate.\r\n* Make your own choice…. You can opt for Scuba Diving/ Kayaking/ Candid Photography at additional cost, booking in advance is recommended though our local representative also can assist you.\r\n\r\nDay 3: Havelock – Elephenta Beach\r\nHavelock Island\r\n* Morning, Breakfast and proceed for “Elephenta Beach” also known as Coral Beach.\r\n* Elephenta beach is popular for Snorkelling and other water-based activities such as Jet Ski ride,\r\nBanana Ride, Sea Walk.\r\n* Usually boat operators provide a 5-minute snorkelling experience complimentary, however the\r\nsame cannot be guaranteed\r\n* You reach Elephenta beach via small 11 pax capacity sharing basis boat board at jetty\r\n* You will be allotted a time for boat a day before and you need to get ready accordingly\r\n* Do not forget to carry a water bottle, snacks and changing cloths.\r\n* Important: In case Elephenta Beach is not operational due to weather conditions OR COVID-19 reasons, we will provide a trip to “Kala Patthar Beach” OR We can refund the applicable amount.\r\n\r\nDay 4: Havelock – Port Blair- Day at leisure\r\nPort Blair\r\n* Breakfast, check out and proceed for jetty and onward journey to Port Blair\r\n* Arrival in Port Blair, Transfer to your booked hotel, Day free for shopping/ leisure.\r\n* Other places like Corbin’s Cove Beach/ Chidiya Tapu/ Wandoor Beach/ Museums & Parks can be\r\ncovered at additional cost subject to time and availability (Optional)\r\n\r\nDay 5: Port Blair-North Bay (Coral Island) – Ross Island\r\nPort Blair\r\n* Morning Breakfast, Pickup to water sports complex and board the speed boat\r\n* The historic Ross Island will take you through the era of Japanese and British period\r\n* An entry amount of Rs. 50 for adult and Rs. 25 for child is directly payable at the Island\r\n* North Bay Island is also known as Coral Beach is popular for water-based adventure activities\r\nsuch as Scuba Diving, Snorkelling, Para Sailings, Dolphin Glass Bottom Boat ride, Coral SafariSemi submarine etc.\r\n* In case “Ross & North” not operational due to bad weather conditions or Covid-19 reason, we shall arrange alternative sightseeing, or we will process applicable refund amount\r\n* Evening, you can (Optional- Direct Payment basis) plan Corbin’s Cove Beach, you can experience enthralling Sea Kart boat ride first time in India.\r\n\r\nTour Ends But Sweet Memories Remains Always','','* Mumbai-Port Blair-Mumbai Economy class airfare\r\n* Daily Breakfast\r\n* Sightseeing as per itinerary\r\n* All Monuments, Museums, Cultural Events, and activities fees as per itinerary\r\n* Return airport/ jetty Transfers in AC vehicle as per itinerary\r\n* All Transportation for local sight-seeing tours by AC Vehicle as per itinerary.\r\n* Cruise transfers Port Blair –Neil Island - Havelock – Port Blair by private ferry Subject to\r\navailability (base category)','* Any meal other than that mentioned above\r\n* Expenditure of a personal nature such as drinks, souvenirs and laundry\r\n* Other personal expenses','The airfare is dynamic and subject to change.','2023-06-06','2023-06-11',1,0,0,'2023-05-18 14:45:05','2023-05-18 19:04:34'),(295,697,2841,2,1,0,0,0,'Port Blair Diaries','5 Nights / 6 Days | 3 Nights Port Blair/ 2 Nights Havelock Island\r\n\r\nSuggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1: Arrival – Port Blair – Cellular Jail - Light & Sound Show\r\nPort Blair\r\n* A