u need to get ready accordingly\r\n* Do not forget to carry a water bottle, snacks and changing cloths.\r\n* Important: In case Elephenta Beach is not operational due to weather conditions OR COVID-19 reasons, we will provide a trip to “Kala Patthar Beach” OR We can refund the applicable amount.\r\n\r\nDay 4: Havelock – Port Blair- Day at leisure\r\nPort Blair\r\n* Breakfast, check out and proceed for jetty and onward journey to Port Blair\r\n* Arrival in Port Blair, Transfer to your booked hotel, Day free for shopping/ leisure.\r\n* Other places like Corbin’s Cove Beach/ Chidiya Tapu/ Wandoor Beach/ Museums & Parks can be\r\ncovered at additional cost subject to time and availability (Optional)\r\n\r\nDay 5: Port Blair-North Bay (Coral Island) – Ross Island\r\nPort Blair\r\n* Morning Breakfast, Pickup to water sports complex and board the speed boat\r\n* The historic Ross Island will take you through the era of Japanese and British period\r\n* An entry amount of Rs. 50 for adult and Rs. 25 for child is directly payable at the Island\r\n* North Bay Island is also known as Coral Beach is popular for water-based adventure activities\r\nsuch as Scuba Diving, Snorkelling, Para Sailings, Dolphin Glass Bottom Boat ride, Coral SafariSemi submarine etc.\r\n* In case “Ross & North” not operational due to bad weather conditions or Covid-19 reason, we shall arrange alternative sightseeing, or we will process applicable refund amount\r\n* Evening, you can (Optional- Direct Payment basis) plan Corbin’s Cove Beach, you can experience enthralling Sea Kart boat ride first time in India.\r\n\r\nTour Ends But Sweet Memories Remains Always','','* Delhi-Port Blair-Delhi Economy class airfare\r\n* Daily Breakfast\r\n* Sightseeing as per itinerary\r\n* All Monuments, Museums, Cultural Events, and activities fees as per itinerary\r\n* Return airport/ jetty Transfers in AC vehicle as per itinerary\r\n* All Transportation for local sight-seeing tours by AC Vehicle as per itinerary.\r\n* Cruise transfers Port Blair –Neil Island - Havelock – Port Blair by private ferry Subject to\r\navailability (base category)\r\n\r\n','* Any meal other than that mentioned above\r\n* Expenditure of a personal nature such as drinks, souvenirs and laundry\r\n* Other personal expenses','The airfare is dynamic and subject to change.','2023-06-25','2023-06-30',1,0,0,'2023-05-18 16:00:18','2023-05-18 16:00:40'),(297,698,15526,2,0,0,0,0,'Kashmir Diaries','6 Nights / 7 Days | 4N Srinagar / 2N Pahalgam\r\n\r\nSuggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDAY 1  ARRIVAL + SRINAGAR LOCAL SIGHSEEING (CHECK-IN HOTEL)\r\nOn arrival at Srinagar airport, our representative will meet you to pick you up and transfer to your hotel. Welcome to Srinagar, the Lake City. Begin your tour of \'Exotic Kashmir. After check-in proceed to Local Sightseeing of Srinagar with a tour of Mughal Gardens visiting Cheshmashahi (the royal spring), Nishat (the garden of pleasure), Shalimar (the abode of love), Pari Mahal. Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar.\r\n\r\nDAY 2  SONMARG DAY TRIP  FROM SRINAGAR\r\nAfter breakfast leave from hotel and proceed to Sonamarg \"Golden Meadow\".  Sonmarg lies in Sind Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. Sonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude of Himalayan Lakes. Enjoy horse riding upto Thajiwas glacier and sledge riding on snow (own cost). Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar.\r\n\r\nDAY 3  GULMARG DAY TRIP  FROM SRINAGAR\r\nAfter breakfast leave from hotel and proceed to Gulmarg . Gulmarg is also known as “Meadow Of Flowers “ & has a famous Golf course during summer  (which is one if the highest 18-holes golf course in the world) & Ski Resort during winter. One can enjoy the breathtaking views of snow clad mountains, Gondola (cable car) ride from Gulmarg to Khilanmarg (own cost) to have a real view in natural beauty of the summer and full snow view in winter. You can have a pony ride in the open fields to seven springs (own cost) and to a lake, which remains frozen until June. Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar.\r\n\r\nDAY 4  CHECK-IN AT PAHALGAM (2 NIGHTS STAY)\r\nAfter breakfast check-out from hotel and transfer to Pahalgam hotel, VILLAGE OF SHEPHERDS “ Pahalgam is known as the land of shepherds. The mountain town is located along the bank of River Lidder. Here you can visit many breath taking places enroute visiting the world famous Saffron  growing  fields . Pahalgam is famous for Indian film industry, some trekking routes & also base camp for Amarnath pilgrimage. Day at leisure. Overnight stay at hotel in Pahalgam. \r\n\r\nDAY 5 EXPLORING CHANDANWARI, BETAB VALLEY, AND ARU VALLEY\r\nAfter a satisfying breakfast, enjoy a leisurely day at your own pace. Take the time to relax and indulge in various activities of your choice. Later, return to your comfortable hotel in Pahalgam for an overnight stay.\r\n\r\nRecommendation (At own cost)) :-     \r\n* Visit Chandanwari, Betab Valley, and Aru Valley \r\n* These destinations offer picturesque meadows and stunning scenery\r\n* They serve as starting points for treks to Liddarwat, Kolahoi Glacier, and Tarsar Lake\r\n* Overnight stay at a hotel in Pahalgam\r\n\r\nDAY 6  CHECK-IN AT SRINAGAR HOUSEBOAT\r\nAfter breakfast check-out from hotel and transfer to Srinagar. Upon arrival check-in houseboat. You can enjoy Shikara Ride on  lake for 1 hour and explore the beauty of the lake. Overnight stay at houseboat in Srinagar.\r\n\r\nDAY 7  CHECK-OUT FROM SRINAGAR HOUSEBOAT\r\nAfter breakfast check-out from Srinagar houseboat and transfer to Srinagar Airport to board the flight for onward destination.\r\n\r\nTour Ends But Sweet Memories Remains Always','','* 06 Nights sty in above mentioned hotel \r\n* Daily Breakfast & dinner at hotel.\r\n* Shikara ride.\r\n* Airport/station pick-up and drop facility as confirmed by the travelers. \r\n* Sightseeing by AC Etios (the AC will not operate in hill area)\r\n* Driver Allowances.\r\n* Toll tax and State tax & Parking (Without Guest entry free at Gulmarg & Aru)\r\n* Hotel Taxes\r\n','* Cost of any adventure activities like Gondola Ride, Skiing, Motor Bike, River rafting, Pony / Sledge Ride etc.\r\n* Cost of Union Cab services in Pahalgam, Gulmarg and Sonamarg.\r\n* Guide fees, Camera fees, shopping & any monument entrances. \r\n* Guest Entry Fee at Gulmarg / Aru.\r\n* Entrance fee for Mughal Gardens or for any Park/ Museum/Monument.\r\n* Expenses of personal nature such as laundry, mini bars, etc. \r\n* The cost of chained vehicles from Tangmarg to Gulmarg & Gulmarg to Tangmarg or Sonamarg in case of \r\n  heavy snow. \r\n* Any meal other than that mentioned above\r\n* Expenditure of a personal nature such as drinks, souvenirs and laundry\r\n* Other personal expenses','The airfare is dynamic and subject to change.','2023-06-24','2023-06-30',1,0,0,'2023-05-18 16:38:46','2023-05-19 21:42:17'),(299,701,33,3,0,0,0,0,'Hong Kong Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 (26 Jun 2023 - Monday)\r\n\r\nArrive Hong Kong. Meet and Greet at Airport\r\nTransfer to Hotel and check in ( 1400 hrs - subject to availability)\r\nProceed for Sightseeing of Hong Kong - Visit to Stanley beach and Repluse Bay.  Repulse Bay is a bay in the southern part of Hong Kong Island. It is one of the most expensive residential areas in Hong Kong. \r\nVisit The Peak - with one way peak tram ride. Visit the Sky Terrace and Madame Tussauds. Enjoy panoramic view of Hong Kong from the highest point.  Proceed to TST clock tower to view Symphony of the lights show\r\nGuide Service for Sightseeing\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel\r\n\r\nDay 2 (27 Jun 2023 - Tuesday)\r\n\r\nBreakfast at Hotel\r\n2 Way Transfers to Disneyland ( Open on 27 June due to public holidays)\r\nEntry Ticket to Disneyland- day 01 of 2 day pass\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel\r\n\r\nDay 3 (28 Jun 2023 - Wednesday)\r\n\r\nBreakfast at Hotel\r\n2 Way Transfers to Disneyland \r\nEntry Ticket to Disneyland- day 02 of 2 day pass\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel\r\n\r\nDay 4 (29 Jun 2023 - Thrusday)\r\n\r\nBreakfast at Hotel\r\n2 Way Transfers to Ocean Park\r\nEntry Ticket to ocean park\r\n2 Way Standard Cabin Ticket\r\nOvernight stay at Hotel\r\n\r\nDay 5 (30 Jun 2023 - Friday)\r\n\r\nBreakfast at Hotel\r\nLantau Island with 2 Way CC Ride at Ngong Ping 360 Tour\r\n2 Way Standard Cabin Ticket\r\nOvernight stay at Hotel\r\n\r\nDay 6 (01 Jul 2023 - Saturday)\r\n\r\nBreakfast at Hotel\r\nTransfers from Hong Kong Hotel to Airport','','* Economy class return airfare\r\n* 05 nights hotel accommodation in Hong Kong as listed above with Buffet Breakfast\r\n* All transfers and Sightseeing by Van on private basis\r\n* Hong Kong City tour Sightseeing will be accompanied by Local English speaking guide.\r\n* All Entrance fees for all attractions as per itinerary.\r\n* Travel Insurance','* Guaranteed early check in or late check out.\r\n* Tips and porter-age\r\n* Meals other than specified in the itinerary.  \r\n* Sightseeing tours are not included\r\n* Any expenses of personal nature\r\n* Any services not mentioned in the inclusions list\r\n* Visa\r\n','The rates are subject to change','2023-06-25','2023-07-01',1,0,0,'2023-05-19 18:29:16','2023-05-26 14:35:38'),(300,704,680,3,0,0,0,0,'Mysore Diaries','Mysore: 1 Nights, Coorg: 2 Nights, Ooty: 2 Nights, Kodaikanal: 2 Nights, Madurai: 1 Nights, Rameswaram: 2 Nights, Kanyakumari: 1 Nights (11 N/ 12 D)\r\n\r\nSuggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 (14 Jun 2023 - Wednesday): Bangalore Arrival to Mysore\r\n* Meet & Assist on arrival at Bangalore Airport.\r\n* Transfer from Bangalore to Mysore.\r\n* Check into Hotel Rio Meridian in Mysore.\r\n* Explore attractions such as Mysore Palace, Devaraja Market, Chamundeshwari Temple, Lalitha Mahal Palace, etc.\r\n* Visit Mysore Zoo, Jaganmohan Palace, Melody World Wax Museum, and Chamundi Hills.\r\n* Don\'t miss a visit to the beautiful Brindavan Gardens.\r\n* Overnight stay at Hotel Rio Meridian.\r\n\r\nDay 2 (15 Jun 2023 - Thursday): Mysore to Coorg\r\n* Enjoy breakfast at Hotel Rio Meridian.\r\n* Transfer from Mysore to Coorg.\r\n* Check into Hotel Ministers kourt Coorg.\r\n* Explore the stunning hill views and natural beauty of Coorg.\r\n* Overnight stay at Hotel Ministers kourt Coorg.\r\n\r\nDay 3 (16 Jun 2023 - Friday): Coorg Sightseeing Day 1\r\n* Have breakfast at Hotel Ministers kourt Coorg.\r\n* Go sightseeing in Kodagu (Coorg).\r\n* Visit Madikeri Fort, Omkareshwara Temple, Raja\'s Tomb, and Abbi Falls.\r\n* Enjoy your time in Kodagu.\r\n* Overnight stay at Hotel Ministers kourt Coorg.\r\n\r\nDay 4 (17 Jun 2023 - Saturday): Coorg to Ooty\r\n* Enjoy breakfast at Hotel Ministers kourt Coorg.\r\n* Check out from the hotel and proceed to Ooty.\r\n* On arrival, check into Hotel Vinayaga Inn by Poppys.\r\n* In the afternoon, visit Ooty Lake and Botanical Garden.\r\n* Overnight stay at Hotel Vinayaga Inn by Poppys.\r\n\r\nDay 5 (18 Jun 2023 - Sunday): Ooty Sightseeing Day 2\r\n* Have breakfast at Hotel Vinayaga Inn by Poppys.\r\n* Proceed to Coonoor for sightseeing.\r\n* Visit Sim\'s Park, Lam\'s Rock, Dolphin Nose, Tea Factory, and Doddabetta Peak.\r\n* Overnight stay at Hotel Vinayaga Inn by Poppys.\r\n\r\nDay 6 (19 Jun 2023 - Monday): Ooty to Kodaikanal\r\n* Enjoy breakfast at Hotel Vinayaga Inn by Poppys.\r\n* Check out from the hotel and proceed to Kodaikanal.\r\n* Visit Green Valley View, Pillar Rocks, Dolphin\'s Nose, Murugan Temple, and Pillar Rocks in Kodaikanal.\r\n* Overnight stay at Hotel Apple Valley, Kodaikanal.\r\n\r\nDay 7 (20 Jun 2023 - Tuesday): Kodaikanal Sightseeing Day 2\r\n* Have breakfast at Hotel Apple Valley, Kodaikanal.\r\n* Go sightseeing in Kodaikanal.\r\n* Visit attractions like Pillar Rocks, Bear-Shola Falls, Bryant Park, and Kodai Lake.\r\n* Enjoy the beautiful sights and serene surroundings.\r\n* Overnight stay at Hotel Apple Valley, Kodaikanal.\r\n\r\nDay 8 (21 Jun 2023 - Wednesday): Kodaikanal to Madurai\r\n* Enjoy breakfast at Hotel Apple Valley, Kodaikanal.\r\n* Check out from the hotel and drive to Madurai.\r\n* On arrival, check into Hotel President Madurai.\r\n* In the afternoon, visit Meenakshi Temple and Tirumalai Nayak Palace.\r\n* Overnight stay at Hotel President Madurai.\r\n\r\nDay 9 (22 Jun 2023 - Thursday): Madurai to Rameshwaram via Dhanushkodi\r\n* Have breakfast at Hotel President Madurai.\r\n* Check out from the hotel and proceed towards Rameshwaram via Dhanushkodi.\r\n* Enjoy leisure time and explore the town.\r\n* Overnight stay at Hotel Vinayaga by Poppys.\r\n\r\nDay 10 (23 Jun 2023 - Friday): Rameshwaram Day 2\r\n* Enjoy breakfast at Hotel Vinayaga by Poppys.\r\n* Visit Rameshwaram, a sacred temple town.\r\n* Explore the Ramanathaswamy Temple and other attractions.\r\n* Overnight stay at Hotel Vinayaga by Poppys.\r\n\r\nDay 11 (24 Jun 2023 - Saturday): Rameshwaram to Kanyakumari\r\n* Have breakfast at Hotel Vinayaga by Poppys.\r\n* Check out from the hotel and proceed to Kanyakumari.\r\n* Overnight stay at Hotel The Gopinivas Grand.\r\n\r\nDay 12 (25 Jun 2023 - Sunday):\r\n* Enjoy breakfast at Hotel The Gopinivas Grand.\r\n* Transfer from Kanyakumari to Trivandrum Airport/Railway station for departure.','','* Ahmedabad-Mysore-Ahmedabad Economy class airfare\r\n* Meal plans as indicated on the itinerary\r\n* Accommodation on Twin Sharing Basis\r\n* All Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\n* All Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost\r\n','* All those which are not mentioned above\r\n* Entry Fees To Monuments And Palaces\r\n* Porterage At Hotels And Airports, Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Liquors, Wine, Etc\r\n* All Items Of Personal Nature\r\n* Ayurveda Charges\r\n* All those which are not mentioned above\r\n','The airfare is dynamic and subject to change.','2023-06-14','2023-06-25',1,0,0,'2023-05-20 13:29:54','2023-05-20 15:59:49'),(301,706,15530,2,0,0,0,0,'Port Blair Diaries','5 Nights / 6 Days | 3 Nights Port Blair/ 2 Nights Havelock Island\r\n\r\nSuggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1: Arrival – Port Blair – Cellular Jail - Light & Sound Show\r\nPort Blair\r\n* Arrival, Meet-Greet with our airport representative and Transfer to your booked hotel/ resort\r\n* Evening, visit to historic Cellular Jail followed by Light & Sound Show\r\n* Please note, we will drop guest at parking area near jail and guest must walk around 200 metre\r\nand return after completion of L&S show.\r\n* Guest has to come out after visiting jail and re-enter for L&S show, Guests can walk around the bay side in free time.\r\n* L&S show timing is in between 1800 Hrs- 1900hrs subject to availability\r\n* The free time between jail visit & L&S show can be utilised in self-exploration of illuminated Marina Park and Sea shore area, evenings are pleasant and happening here.\r\n\r\nDay 2: Port Blair- Havelock- Radha Nagar Beach\r\nHavelock Island\r\n* Pick up from hotel to Port Blair Jetty for your onward journey to Havelock\r\n* If you have morning ferry, ask hotel to provide Packed breakfast (Subject to hotel policy)\r\n* Arrival, Meet- Greet by our local representative and transfer to your booked hotel/ Resort\r\n* Afternoon, Visit to Blue Flag certified “Radha Nagar Beach” for swim and relaxation.\r\n* Do not forget to carry changing cloths and towel\r\n* It’s not permitted to board vehicle with wet cloths, please cooperate.\r\n* Make your own choice…. You can opt for Scuba Diving/ Kayaking/ Candid Photography at additional cost, booking in advance is recommended though our local representative also can assist you.\r\n\r\nDay 3: Havelock – Elephenta Beach\r\nHavelock Island\r\n* Morning, Breakfast and proceed for “Elephenta Beach” also known as Coral Beach.\r\n* Elephenta beach is popular for Snorkelling and other water-based activities such as Jet Ski ride,\r\nBanana Ride, Sea Walk.\r\n* Usually boat operators provide a 5-minute snorkelling experience complimentary, however the\r\nsame cannot be guaranteed\r\n* You reach Elephenta beach via small 11 pax capacity sharing basis boat board at jetty\r\n* You will be allotted a time for boat a day before and you need to get ready accordingly\r\n* Do not forget to carry a water bottle, snacks and changing cloths.\r\n* Important: In case Elephenta Beach is not operational due to weather conditions OR COVID-19 reasons, we will provide a trip to “Kala Patthar Beach” OR We can refund the applicable amount.\r\n\r\nDay 4: Havelock – Port Blair- Day at leisure\r\nPort Blair\r\n* Breakfast, check out and proceed for jetty and onward journey to Port Blair\r\n* Arrival in Port Blair, Transfer to your booked hotel, Day free for shopping/ leisure.\r\n* Other places like Corbin’s Cove Beach/ Chidiya Tapu/ Wandoor Beach/ Museums & Parks can be\r\ncovered at additional cost subject to time and availability (Optional)\r\n\r\nDay 5: Port Blair-North Bay (Coral Island) – Ross Island\r\nPort Blair\r\n* Morning Breakfast, Pickup to water sports complex and board the speed boat\r\n* The historic Ross Island will take you through the era of Japanese and British period\r\n* An entry amount of Rs. 50 for adult and Rs. 25 for child is directly payable at the Island\r\n* North Bay Island is also known as Coral Beach is popular for water-based adventure activities\r\nsuch as Scuba Diving, Snorkelling, Para Sailings, Dolphin Glass Bottom Boat ride, Coral SafariSemi submarine etc.\r\n* In case “Ross & North” not operational due to bad weather conditions or Covid-19 reason, we shall arrange alternative sightseeing, or we will process applicable refund amount\r\n* Evening, you can (Optional- Direct Payment basis) plan Corbin’s Cove Beach, you can experience enthralling Sea Kart boat ride first time in India.\r\n\r\nTour Ends But Sweet Memories Remains Always','','* Delhi-Port Blair-Delhi Economy class airfare\r\n* Daily Breakfast\r\n* Sightseeing as per itinerary\r\n* All Monuments, Museums, Cultural Events, and activities fees as per itinerary\r\n* Return airport/ jetty Transfers in AC vehicle as per itinerary\r\n* All Transportation for local sight-seeing tours by AC Vehicle as per itinerary.\r\n* Cruise transfers Port Blair –Neil Island - Havelock – Port Blair by private ferry Subject to\r\navailability (base category)\r\n','* Any meal other than that mentioned above\r\n* Expenditure of a personal nature such as drinks, souvenirs and laundry\r\n* Other personal expenses','The airfare is dynamic and subject to change.','2023-07-04','2023-07-09',1,0,0,'2023-05-20 15:01:48','2023-05-20 15:01:48'),(302,707,16002,2,0,0,68000,21200,'Bali Diaries','6 Nights Bali Stay with transfers and sightseeing.\r\n\r\nSuggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 (05 Jul 2023 - Wednesday)\r\nTransfer in to Select Hotel 	 \r\nPick up from Airport and drop to Hotel \r\n\r\nDay 2 (06 Jul 2023 - Thrusday)\r\nTanjung Benoa Water Sports + Uluwatu Tour\r\nwater creation center (carry 1 pair of cloth with you)	 \r\n1 Round Banana Boat	 \r\n[other activities on your own account]	 \r\nUluwatu Temple\r\n\r\nDay 3 (07 Jul 2023 - Friday)\r\nBreakfast at the hotel. Pick up early morning at hotel for Nusa Penida West Island Tour with\r\n06.30 AM : Driver pick up time from your hotel (depending of the hotel location)	 \r\nVisit -Crystal bay, Broken beach ,Angel billabong, Lunch at Local Restaurant.	 \r\nKelingkinhg Kliff, Kelingkinhg Kliff Selfie, \r\n\r\nDay 4 (08 Jul 2023 - Saturday)\r\nBedugul + Tanah lot tour	\r\nBedugul - ulun danu temple at britain lake 	 \r\nTanha lot temple \r\n\r\nDay 5 (09 Jul 2023 - Sunday)\r\nInter Hotel Transfer + Kintamani + Ubud Tour	\r\nFull Day Tour Visit:Mas/Celuk for local art & craft market	 \r\ncontinue visit Kintmani mount batur volcano, Spices Garden and Ubud Market	 \r\nTegalalang rice terrace 	 \r\n 	 \r\nDay 6 (10 Jul 2023 - Monday)\r\nDay at leisure \r\n\r\nDay 7 (11 Jul 2023 - Tuesday)\r\nTransfer Out','','* Delhi-Bali-Delhi Economy class airfare	\r\n* All Transfer on private basis\r\n* Travel Insurance\r\n* Inter hotel transfer on private basis\r\n* Daily Breakfast \r\n* One Lunch at Local Restaurant','* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Any surcharge at the hotel (Mini bar, \r\n  Visiter fee ect.)\r\n* Other personal expenses\r\n* Surcharge for peak season if any (Upon \r\n  booking)\r\n* Expenditure of a personal nature such as \r\n  drinks, souvenirs and laundry\r\n* TCS','The airfare is dynamic and subject to change.','2023-07-04','2023-07-11',1,0,0,'2023-05-20 16:46:52','2023-05-20 17:01:19'),(303,708,15512,2,1,0,0,0,'5D/4N NORTHERN VIETNAM TOUR','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 1- Hanoi Arrival - city highlights (-/-/-)\r\nDay 2- Ninh Binh day trip (B/L/-) - SIC\r\nDay 3- Hanoi – Halong Bay (B/L/D) - SIC tour\r\nDay 4- Halong Bay – Hanoi (Brunch/-)\r\nDay 5- Hanoi Departure (B/-/-)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 1 - Wed 01 Mar 2023: Hanoi Arrival - city highlights (-/-/-)\r\nWelcome to Hanoi, the capital city of Vietnam. Upon arrival, greeted by the local tour guide and transfer to downtown. Check in your hotel. Afternoon, visit Ba Dinh Square – the biggest square in Hanoi where all the biggest cultural, political events of the cities, especially demonstrations, take place. Start our visit at the Complex of Ho Chi Minh including Ho Chi Minh Mausoleum (from outside only as it closes in the afternoon), Ho Chi Minh’s house-on-stilts, his fish pond and the One-Pillar Pagoda. Then, the Temple of Literature which is considered as the first university of Vietnam.\r\nLater, we have an overall view of the capital by cyclo in 1 hour, which wanders around the Old Quarter of Hanoi and the Hoan Kiem Lake (the “Sword” Lake). From here wandering on the narrow streets of the Old Quarter to experience the daily life of the local people. Transfer back to your hotel. Overnight in Hanoi. Please note: the standard check in time is\r\n14:00 – 15:00pm. Early check in is not included and subject to hotel availability. Night activities suggestion: enjoy local beer at Ta Hien Streets, experience the ambience of sleepless street with life music, the young people of Hanoi and also foreign tourists. Hundred of bars and pubs in the Old Quarter are also at your disposal Or just simple spend your time at shopping malls or various boutique Shops.\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 2 - Thu 02 Mar 2023: Ninh Binh day trip (B/L/-) - SIC\r\n\r\n7:15-7:45am Our driver and tour guide pick you up at hotels in the Old Quarter Area, Hanoi. Head the south of Hanoi for 110 km. After 2 hours, you will arrive in Ninh Binh. First stop at Hoa Lu, you will have quick visit two temples built in honor of the emperors Dinh Le, their sons, and the Queen... to know why Hoa Lu was build as capital of Vietnam in ending of nine century.\r\n\r\n12:00 – Enjoy lunch at our restaurant with the great local cuisine.\r\n\r\n13:30 – Boarding a small sampan to visit Tam Coc which means literally “three caves” (1.5 hour boat trip). With Halong bay type views of majestic limestone cliffs and mysterious caves, as well as countryside landscape like peaceful streams, rice paddies and deserted green fields, Tam Coc really has it all. You will feel the fresh air and peaceful moments, very good opportunities for photo lovers, freezing the special moments and scenery.\r\n\r\n17:15 – Return to our bus and then come back to Ha Noi\r\n\r\n19:30 – Drop you off at your hotel/stay. Trip ends.\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 3 - Fri 03 Mar 2023: Hanoi – Halong Bay (B/L/D) - SIC tour\r\n08.00-09.00: Shuttles bus pick up and departure in the morning from Hanoi. We drive across the Red River delta and reach the coast a little before noon. We then embark on a beautifully crafted junk for an overnight cruise in the legendary seascape of Ha Long Bay. Once on board, we are served a delicious seafood-based lunch, while the surrounding limestone outcrops make for a truly magical setting. In the afternoon, we reach a less travelled area where we will devote ourselves to pure relaxation. The program is not fixed and depends on the time of the year and weather, but there will be an opportunity to visit a cave as well as explore a floating village or do a little bit of kayaking over the course of these 2 days. We end the day on the sundeck as the sun sets on this magical seascape. This evening, you can enjoy an aperitif or attend a cooking demonstration before dinner. Overnight in a comfortable private cabin with an en-suite bathroom.\r\n\r\nNote: Cruise itinerary and schedule are subject to change due to weather, tide levels and operating conditions. Swimming or kayaking excursions may be cancelled due to poor weather.\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 4 - Sat 04 Mar 2023: Halong Bay – Hanoi (Brunch/-)\r\nFor those early birds, start the day with a proposed Tai Chi session, while tea and coffee are served as the sun rises and illuminates the surrounding seascape. We then continue our exploration of the bay. Upon returning to the boat, check-out of your cabin and enjoy a light brunch while cruising back to the pier. We disembark and transfer back to Hanoi.\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 5 - Sun 05 Mar 2023: Hanoi Departure (B/-/-)\r\nThe day is free at your leisure until transfer without guide to Noi Bai International Airport for your departure flight. We wish you a pleasant flight!\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Return Airfare (Delhi - Hanoi - Delhi)\r\n* Accommodation in twin/double room with daily breakfast\r\n* 2Days/1Night cruise on board a cruise in Ha Long Bay (private cabin on shared boat).\r\n* Boat trip - as per program\r\n* All entrance fees - as per program\r\n* Shuttle bus from/to Hanoi - Ha Long- Ha Long\r\n* Government tax and service charge\r\n* Bottles of mineral water on tour day\r\n* Meals (B/L/D) (Breakfast/Lunch/Dinner) as indicated in the program\r\n* Local ENGLISH speaking guides\r\n* Enjoy lunch at a local restaurant\r\n* All transfers and transportation with Air-Con vehicles\r\n* Travel Insurance\r\n','* Early check-in or late check-out\r\n* Optional excursions and activities\r\n* Drinks\r\n* Meals (other than mentioned in the program)\r\n* Additional transfer required due to any emergency situation\r\n* Items of a personal nature (Phone calls, laundry, beverages, etc.)\r\n* Mineral water beyond that which is supplied\r\n* Surcharge for peak season if any (Upon booking)\r\n* TCS\r\n\r\n ','The airfare is dynamic and subject to change.','2023-06-19','2023-06-24',1,0,0,'2023-05-22 19:55:24','2023-05-23 15:11:45'),(304,709,15506,2,1,0,0,0,'Turkey Diaries','6 Nights / 7 Days | 3N Istanbul / 3N Cappadocia \r\n\r\nISTANBUL (COMFORT 4 STAR OPTIONS)\r\nRamada Grand Bazaar // Nova Plaza Crystal // Metropolitan Taksim // Golden Age // Elite World Comfy // Nippon OR Similar Hotel\r\n\r\nCAPPADOCIA (COMFORT 4 Star OPTIONS)\r\nSelcuklu Evi Cave // Dedeli Konak Cave // Doors of Cappadocia // Alfina Cave // Mithra Cave // Fresco Cave OR Similar Hotel\r\n\r\nISTANBUL (LUXURY 5 STAR OPTIONS)\r\nSura Hagia Sophia // Crown Plaza Old City // Crown Plaza Harbiye // Radisson Blu Pera // Elite World Istanbul // Point Hotel OR Similar Hotel\r\n\r\nCAPPADOCIA (LUXURY 5 Star OPTIONS)\r\nMDC Cave // Exedra Cave // Elika Cave Suites // Dere Suites // Utopia Cave OR Similar Hotel\r\n\r\n\r\nSuggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n\r\nDAY 1: ISTANBUL\r\nArrival to Istanbul and transfer to the hotel. Free rest of the day. Overnight in Istanbul.\r\n\r\nDAY 2: ISTANBUL\r\nAfter breakfast, depart for a full-day tour of Istanbul. Visit Blue Mosque, Hagia Sophia, Hippodrome, Grand Bazaar, Topkapi Palace and Sultans’ Tombs. Overnight in Istanbul.\r\n\r\nDAY 3: ISTANBUL\r\nAfter breakfast, visit Egyptian Bazaar (spice bazaar) and cruise along the Bosphorus. Lunch. Beylerbeyi Palace visit which is summer residence of Ottoman Sultans. Then Camlica Hill. Highest point of Istanbul. Overnight in Istanbul.\r\n \r\nDAY 4: ISTANBUL/CAPPADOCIA\r\nAfter breakfast, transfer to the airport for the flight to Kayseri/Nevsehir. Arrival and transfer to the hotel. Dinner and overnight in Cappadocia.\r\n\r\nDAY 5: CAPPADOCIA\r\nAfter breakfast depart for Cappadocia North Tour. Visit Dervent Valley, Pasabag fairy chimneys, Avanos, Goreme open air museum and Uchisar rock castle. Dinner and overnight in Cappadocia.\r\n\r\nDAY 6: CAPPADOCIA\r\nAfter breakfast depart for Cappadocia South Tour. Visit Red Valley, Pigeon Valley, Cavusin Village, Underground City. Dinner and overnight in Cappadocia\r\n\r\nDAY 7: CAPPADOCIA/AIRPORT\r\nAfter breakfast, transfer to the airport for the flight to Istanbul to take the international flight.\r\n,ITINERARY\r\nDAY 1: ISTANBUL\r\nArrival to Istanbul and transfer to the hotel. Free rest of the day. Overnight in Istanbul.\r\n\r\nDAY 2: ISTANBUL\r\nAfter breakfast, depart for a full-day tour of Istanbul. Visit Blue Mosque, Hagia Sophia, Hippodrome, Grand Bazaar, Topkapi Palace and Sultans’ Tombs. Overnight in Istanbul.\r\n\r\nDAY 3: ISTANBUL\r\nAfter breakfast, visit Egyptian Bazaar (spice bazaar) and cruise along the Bosphorus. Lunch. Beylerbeyi Palace visit which is summer residence of Ottoman Sultans. Then Camlica Hill. Highest point of Istanbul. Overnight in Istanbul.\r\n \r\nDAY 4: ISTANBUL/CAPPADOCIA\r\nAfter breakfast, transfer to the airport for the flight to Kayseri/Nevsehir. Arrival and transfer to the hotel. Dinner and overnight in Cappadocia.\r\n\r\nDAY 5: CAPPADOCIA\r\nAfter breakfast depart for Cappadocia North Tour. Visit Dervent Valley, Pasabag fairy chimneys, Avanos, Goreme open air museum and Uchisar rock castle. Dinner and overnight in Cappadocia.\r\n\r\nDAY 6: CAPPADOCIA\r\nAfter breakfast depart for Cappadocia South Tour. Visit Red Valley, Pigeon Valley, Cavusin Village, Underground City. Dinner and overnight in Cappadocia\r\n\r\nDAY 7: CAPPADOCIA/AIRPORT\r\nAfter breakfast, transfer to the airport for the flight to Istanbul to take the international flight.','','* Economy Class Return Airfare (Delhi - Istanbul - Delhi)\r\n* Economy Class Return Airfare (Istanbul - Nevsehir - Istanbul)\r\n* 03 Nights in Istanbul at Selected Category of Hotel OR Similar on BB basis \r\n* 03 Nights in Cappadocia at Selected Category of Hotel OR Similar on HB basis\r\n* R/T Transfer in Istanbul (IST AIRPORT) and Cappadocia on PVT basis.\r\n* FD Istanbul Old City Tour with Local lunch on SIC basis.\r\n* FD Bosphorus & 2 Continents Tour with lunch on SIC basis.\r\n* FD Cappadocia North tour with Local Lunch on SIC basis.\r\n* FD Cappadocia South tour with Local Lunch on SIC basis.\r\n* Entrance Fees	\r\n* Travel Insurance','* Optional excursions and activities\r\n* Meals (other than mentioned in the program)\r\n* Items of a personal nature (Phone calls, laundry, beverages, etc.)\r\n* Surcharge for peak season if any (Upon booking)\r\n* TCS','The airfare is dynamic and subject to change.','2023-06-18','2023-06-25',1,0,0,'2023-05-23 16:24:29','2023-05-23 18:58:36'),(305,710,54,2,1,0,0,0,'Singapore Diaries','\r\nTransports and Activities\r\n\r\n1st Day (3 Aug)\r\nSingapore - Airport Arrival Transfer - 1 PRIVATE COMBI\r\nNight Safari Transfer - Return Transfers - SIC (Night Safari Ticket Only)\r\n\r\n2nd Day (4 Aug)\r\nSingapore Half Day City Orientation Drive - SIC\r\nGardens By The Bay - Return Transfers - SIC (Cloud Forest + Flower Dome Ticket Only)\r\n\r\n3rd Day (5 Aug)\r\nUniversal Studios Return Transfers- SIC (Universal Studio Ticket Only)\r\n\r\n4th Day (6 Aug)\r\nSentosa Afternoon Return Transfers- SIC\r\nSentosa Attractions Ticket (Combo 2 - Cable Car + Madame Tussauds Combo (5 in 1) + WOT)\r\n\r\n5th Day (7 Aug)\r\nDay at leisure\r\n\r\n6th Day (8 Aug)\r\nSingapore - Airport Departure Transfer (1 PRIVATE COMBI)\r\n\r\n','','Economy class return airfare\r\n5 nights stay in the mentioned hotel\r\n5 breakfasts\r\nAirport transfers\r\nTours and sightseeing as mentioned in the itinerary\r\nVisa Charges\r\nTravel Insurance\r\n','Any type of personal expense \r\nAny expense due to natural calamity or change in flight\r\nAny meal other than mentioned above\r\nAnything which is not mentioned in inclusions\r\nTCS','The rates are subject to change','2023-08-02','2023-08-08',1,0,0,'2023-05-23 17:15:03','2023-05-23 18:52:29'),(306,712,54,5,0,0,0,0,'Singapore Diaries','\r\nTransports and Activities\r\n\r\n1st Day (7 June)\r\nSingapore - Airport Arrival Transfer - 1 PRIVATE COMBI\r\nNight Safari Transfer - Return Transfers - SIC (Night Safari Ticket Only)\r\n\r\n2nd Day (8 June)\r\nSingapore Half Day City Orientation Drive - SIC\r\nGardens By The Bay - Return Transfers - SIC (Cloud Forest + Flower Dome Ticket Only)\r\n\r\n3rd Day (9 June)\r\nSentosa Afternoon Return Transfers- SIC\r\nSentosa Attractions Ticket (Combo 2 - Cable Car + Madame Tussauds Combo (5 in 1) + WOT)\r\n\r\n4th Day (10 June)\r\nUniversal Studios Return Transfers- SIC (Universal Studio Ticket Only)\r\n\r\n5th Day (11 June)\r\nDay at leisure\r\n\r\n6th Day (12 June)\r\nSingapore - Airport Departure Transfer (1 PRIVATE COMBI)\r\n\r\n','','Economy class return airfare\r\n5 nights stay in the mentioned hotel\r\n5 breakfasts\r\nAirport transfers\r\nTours and sightseeing as mentioned in the itinerary\r\nVisa Charges\r\nTravel Insurance','Any type of personal expense \r\nAny expense due to natural calamity or change in flight\r\nAny meal other than mentioned above\r\nAnything which is not mentioned in inclusions\r\nTCS','The rates are subject to change','2023-06-07','2023-06-12',1,0,0,'2023-05-24 00:08:19','2023-05-24 17:59:25'),(307,713,54,2,0,0,144000,35000,'Singapore Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 01 -Arrive - Singapore\r\nSingapore - a sunny, tropical island in Southeast Asia, off the southern tip of the Malay Peninsula. Singapore, officially the\r\nRepublic of Singapore, is known as the Lion City (Singapura) .On arrival pick up from airport and transfer to hotel.\r\n(Standard check in time is 14:00 to 15:00 PM). \r\nIn Evening pick up from hotel lobby and proceed to Night Safari - the world\'s first\r\nnocturnal zoo and is one of the most popular tourist attractions in Singapore. The Night Safari currently houses over 900\r\nanimals representing over 100 species, of which 41% are threatened species.\r\nOvernight at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 02 - Singapore\r\nBreakfast at hotel.\r\nPick up from Hotel lobby and proceed to Universal Studios- Singapore is Southeast\r\nAsia\'s first and only movie theme park, features thrilling attractions, rides and entertainment for everyone.\r\nOvernight at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 03- Singapore- City tour- Cruise\r\nBreakfast at hotel.\r\nAfter breakfast at Hotel, pick up from hotel lobby and proceed for Singapore city tour- visit Central district Orchard road,\r\nvisit at Chinese temple in China town, Merlion park at marina bay (photo stop only).\r\nAround 4pm , pick up from hotel and transfer to Cruise terminal.\r\nCruise sailing starts at 8 pm.\r\nOnBoard Cruise\r\n\r\nDay 04 - Cruise\r\nOnBoard Cruise/ High Seas\r\n\r\nDay 05- Singapore\r\nCruise arrives back to Singapore at 10:00 am.\r\nPick up from Cruise terminal and transfer to hotel.\r\nAfternoon pick up for Sentosa island tour- offers a variety of attractions to provide variety of experiences, recreation & entertainment to visitors. \r\nSky ride - a chair lift which offers bird eye view of Sentosa island. \r\nLuge ride - features a self steering, gravity driven three wheel cart, Cable car, 4D Adventure, SEA Aquarium, Wings of time.\r\nOvernight at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 06- Singapore Departure\r\nEnjoy breakfast at Hotel. Day at leisure.\r\n(Standard hotel check out time: 12pm)\r\nPick up from hotel lobby and transfer to airport for flight back to Surat.','','* Accommodation at the hotels mentioned or similar.\r\n* 03 nights Singapore stay with breakfast\r\n* 02 nights stay on Cruise (Genting Dream Cruise-Inside Stateroom)\r\n* All meals on Cruise\r\n* Airport - hotel- airport transfers\r\n* Hotel- cruise terminal- hotel transfers\r\n* Night safari tour\r\n* Universal Studio tour\r\n* Sentosa Island tour with wings of time, sky ride, luge ride, 4d adventure, cable car, SEA Aquarium\r\n* Singapore city tour-03 hrs approx\r\n* All transfers & tours on seat in coach/ sharing basis\r\n* Singapore Visa Charges\r\n* Port charges\r\n* One time pick up & delivery is included.','* Dinner & Lunch\r\n* Gratuity of Cruise to be paid directly onboard cruise SGD 21 per person per night\r\n* Cost for shore excursion on port of halt of Cruise\r\n* Door step delivery/ Pick up (Document & Payment Collection charges)-Pay Rs 700 per visit\r\n* TCS\r\n','','2023-06-26','2023-07-03',1,0,0,'2023-05-24 18:13:58','2023-05-24 18:45:31'),(308,714,54,2,0,0,57100,13000,'Singapore Diaries','\r\nTransports and Activities\r\n\r\n1st Day (30 June)\r\nSingapore - Airport Arrival Transfer - 1 PRIVATE COMBI\r\nNight Safari Transfer - Return Transfers - SIC (Night Safari Ticket Only)\r\n\r\n2nd Day (1 July)\r\nSingapore Half Day City Orientation Drive - SIC\r\nGardens By The Bay - Return Transfers - SIC (Flower Dome + Supertree Ticket Only) \r\n\r\n3rd Day (2 July)\r\nSentosa Afternoon Return Transfers- SIC\r\nSentosa Attractions Ticket (Combo 2 - Cable Car + Madame Tussauds Combo (5 in 1) + WOT)\r\n\r\n4th Day (3 July)\r\nUniversal Studios Return Transfers- SIC (Universal Studio Ticket Only)\r\n\r\n5th Day (4 July)\r\nDay at leisure\r\n\r\n6th Day (5 July)\r\nSingapore - Airport Departure Transfer (1 PRIVATE COMBI)\r\n\r\n','','Economy class return airfare\r\n5 nights stay in the mentioned hotel\r\n5 breakfasts\r\nAirport transfers\r\nTours and sightseeing as mentioned in the itinerary\r\nVisa Charges\r\nTravel Insurance','Any type of personal expense \r\nAny expense due to natural calamity or change in flight\r\nAny meal other than mentioned above\r\nAnything which is not mentioned in inclusions\r\nTCS','The rates are subject to change','2023-06-30','2023-07-05',1,0,0,'2023-05-25 09:14:18','2023-05-25 09:14:18'),(309,715,54,2,0,0,38200,9000,'Singapore Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n1st Day (24 June)\r\nSingapore - Airport Arrival Transfer - PRIVATE\r\nGardens by the Bay (Flower Dome + Supertree)\r\nReturn Transfers - SIC \r\n\r\n2nd Day (25 June)\r\nSingapore City Orientation Drive and Night Safari with Tram Ride\r\nReturn Transfers - SIC \r\n\r\n3rd Day (26 June) \r\nSentosa Tour (Inclusion Cable Car,Luge & Skyride,Wings of Time)\r\nReturn Transfers - SIC  \r\n\r\n4th Day (27 June)\r\nUniversal Studio\r\nReturn Transfers - SIC  \r\n\r\n5th Day (28 June)\r\nDay at leisure\r\n\r\n6th Day (29 June)\r\nSingapore - Airport Departure Transfer - PRIVATE','','Economy class return airfare\r\n5 nights stay in the mentioned hotel\r\n5 breakfasts\r\nAirport transfers\r\nTours and sightseeing as mentioned in the itinerary\r\nVisa Charges\r\nTravel Insurance','Any type of personal expense\r\nAny expense due to natural calamity or change in flight\r\nAny meal other than mentioned above\r\nAnything which is not mentioned in inclusions\r\nTCS\r\n\r\n','The rates are subject to change','2023-06-23','2023-06-29',1,0,0,'2023-05-25 16:28:47','2023-05-25 16:53:35'),(310,717,15526,2,1,0,50000,18000,'Kashmir Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 - ARRIVAL + SRINAGAR LOCAL SIGHSEEING (CHECK-IN HOTEL)\r\nOn arrival at Srinagar airport, our representative will meet you to pick you up and transfer to your hotel. Welcome to Srinagar, the Lake City. Begin your tour of \'Exotic Kashmir. After check-in proceed to Local Sightseeing of Srinagar with a tour of Mughal Gardens visiting Cheshmashahi (the royal spring), Nishat (the garden of pleasure), Shalimar (the abode of love), Pari Mahal. Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar.\r\n\r\nDay 2 - SONMARG DAY TRIP  FROM SRINAGAR\r\nAfter breakfast leave from hotel and proceed to Sonamarg \"Golden Meadow\".  Sonmarg lies in Sind Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. Sonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude of Himalayan Lakes. Enjoy horse riding upto Thajiwas glacier and sledge riding on snow (own cost). Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar.\r\n\r\nDay 3 - CHECK-IN AT GULMARG (1 NIGHT STAY)	 	\r\nAfter breakfast leave from hotel and proceed to Gulmarg . Gulmarg is also known as “Meadow Of Flowers “ & has a famous Golf course during summer  (which is one if the highest 18-holes golf course in the world) & Ski Resort during winter. One can enjoy the breathtaking views of snow clad mountains, Gondola (cable car) ride from Gulmarg to Khilanmarg (own cost) to have a real view in natural beauty of the summer and full snow view in winter. You can have a pony ride in the open fields to seven springs (own cost) and to a lake, which remains frozen until June. Overnight stay at hotel in Gulmarg.	 	\r\n		\r\nDay  4 - CHECK-IN AT PAHALGAM (1 NIGHT STAY)	 	\r\nAfter breakfast check-out from hotel and transfer to Pahalgam hotel, VILLAGE OF SHEPHERDS “ Pahalgam is known as the land of shepherds. The mountain town is located along the bank of River Lidder. Here you can visit many breath taking places enroute visiting the world famous Saffron  growing  fields . Pahalgam is famous for Indian film industry, some trekking routes & also base camp for Amarnath pilgrimage. One can visit chandanwari,  Betab Valley and Aru Valley (own cost) has a fine Meadows of Picturesque scenery & starting point of trekking of Liddarwat , Kolahoi Glacier , Tarsar Lake. Overnight stay at hotel in Pahalgam.	 	\r\n		\r\nDay 5 - CHECK-IN AT SRINAGAR HOUSEBOAT\r\nAfter breakfast check-out from hotel and transfer to Srinagar. Upon arrival check-in houseboat. After rest in evening enjoy Shikara Ride on Dal lake for 1 hour and explore the beauty of the lake. Overnight stay at houseboat in Srinagar.\r\n\r\nDay 6 - CHECK-OUT FROM SRINAGAR HOUSEBOAT\r\nAfter breakfast check-out from Srinagar houseboat and transfer to Srinagar Airport to board the flight for onward destination.','','* Economy class return airfare\r\n* Accommodation  as above.\r\n* Daily Breakfast and Dinner in the hotel.\r\n* Airport - pick-up and drop facility on pvt basis. \r\n* Sightseeing by non-AC vehicle on pvt basis\r\n* Shikara Ride (01 hour) will be given in same houseboat\r\n* Driver Allowances.\r\n* Toll tax and State tax & Parking (Without Guest entry free at Gulmarg & Aru)\r\n* Hotel Taxes\r\n','* Cost of any adventure activities like Gondola Ride, Skiing, Motor Bike, River rafting, Pony / Sledge Ride etc.\r\n* Cost of Union Cab services in Pahalgam, Gulmarg and Sonamarg.\r\n* Guide fees, Camera fees, shopping & any monument entrances. \r\n* Guest Entry Fee at Gulmarg / Aru.\r\n* Entrance fee for Mughal Gardens or for any Park/ Museum/Monument.\r\n* Expenses of personal nature such as laundry, mini bars, etc. \r\n* The cost of chained vehicles from Tangmarg to Gulmarg & Gulmarg to Tangmarg or Sonamarg in case of heavy snow. \r\n\r\n','The rates are subject to change','2023-06-13','2023-06-19',1,0,0,'2023-05-25 17:36:06','2023-05-25 19:12:50'),(311,719,54,2,0,0,38200,9000,'Singapore Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n1st Day (24 June)\r\nSingapore - Airport Arrival Transfer - PRIVATE\r\nGardens by the Bay (Flower Dome + Supertree)\r\nReturn Transfers - SIC \r\n\r\n2nd Day (25 June)\r\nSingapore City Orientation Drive and Night Safari with Tram Ride\r\nReturn Transfers - SIC \r\n\r\n3rd Day (26 June) \r\nSentosa Tour (Inclusion Cable Car,Luge & Skyride,Wings of Time)\r\nReturn Transfers - SIC  \r\n\r\n4th Day (27 June)\r\nUniversal Studio\r\nReturn Transfers - SIC  \r\n\r\n5th Day (28 June)\r\nDay at leisure\r\n\r\n6th Day (29 June)\r\nSingapore - Airport Departure Transfer - PRIVATE','','Economy class return airfare\r\n5 nights stay in the mentioned hotel\r\n5 breakfasts\r\nAirport transfers\r\nTours and sightseeing as mentioned in the itinerary\r\nVisa Charges\r\nTravel Insurance','Any type of personal expense\r\nAny expense due to natural calamity or change in flight\r\nAny meal other than mentioned above\r\nAnything which is not mentioned in inclusions\r\nTCS\r\n\r\n','The rates are subject to change','2023-06-23','2023-06-29',1,0,0,'2023-05-25 18:14:24','2023-05-25 18:14:24'),(312,720,15526,4,0,0,66800,18000,'Kashmir Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 01: On arrival at Srinagar airport, our representative will meet you to pick you up and transfer to your hotel. Welcome to Srinagar, the Lake City. Begin your tour of \'Exotic Kashmir. After check-in proceed to Local Sightseeing of Srinagar with a tour of Mughal Gardens visiting Cheshmashahi (the royal spring), Nishat (the garden of pleasure), Shalimar (the abode of love), Pari Mahal. Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar.\r\n\r\nDay 02: After breakfast leave from hotel and proceed to Gulmarg . Gulmarg is also known as “Meadow Of Flowers “ & has a famous Golf course during summer  (which is one if the highest 18-holes golf course in the world) & Ski Resort during winter. One can enjoy the breathtaking views of snow clad mountains, Gondola (cable car) ride from Gulmarg to Khilanmarg (own cost) to have a real view in natural beauty of the summer and full snow view in winter. You can have a pony ride in the open fields to seven springs (own cost) and to a lake, which remains frozen until June. Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar.\r\n\r\nDay 03: After breakfast check-out from hotel and transfer to Pahalgam hotel, VILLAGE OF SHEPHERDS “ Pahalgam is known as the land of shepherds. The mountain town is located along the bank of River Lidder. Here you can visit many breath taking places enroute visiting the world famous Saffron  growing  fields . Pahalgam is famous for Indian film industry, some trekking routes & also base camp for Amarnath pilgrimage. Day at leisure. Overnight stay at hotel in Pahalgam.\r\n\r\nDay 04: After breakfast one can visit chandanwari,  Betab Valley and Aru Valley (own cost) has a fine Meadows of Picturesque scenery & starting point of trekking of Liddarwat , Kolahoi Glacier , Tarsar Lake. Overnight stay at hotel in Pahalgam.\r\n\r\nDay 05: After breakfast check-out from hotel and transfer to Srinagar. Upon arrival check-in houseboat. After rest in evening enjoy Shikara Ride for 1 hour and explore the beauty of the lake. Overnight stay at houseboat in Srinagar.\r\n\r\nDay 06: After breakfast check-out from Srinagar houseboat and transfer to Srinagar Airport to board the flight for onward destination.','','* Economy class return airfare\r\n* Accommodation on Twin/ Double sharing basis\r\n* Airport/station pick-up and drop facility as confirmed by the travelers. \r\n* Sightseeing by Non – Ac Innova\r\n* Cost of Shikara Ride.\r\n* Driver Allowances.\r\n* Toll tax and State tax & Parking (Without Guest entry fee at Gulmarg & Aru)\r\n* Hotel Taxes\r\n','* Cost of any adventure activities like Gondola Ride, Skiing, Motor Bike, River rafting, Pony / Sledge Ride etc.\r\n* Cost of Union Cab services in Pahalgam, Gulmarg and Sonamarg.\r\n* Guide fees, Camera fees, shopping & any monument entrances.\r\n* Guest Entry Fee at Gulmarg / Aru.\r\n* Entrance fee for Mughal Gardens or for any Park/ Museum/Monument.\r\n* Expenses of personal nature such as laundry, mini bars, etc.\r\n* The cost of chained vehicles from Tangmarg to Gulmarg & Gulmarg to Tangmarg or Sonamarg in case of heavy snow.','','2023-06-25','2023-06-30',1,0,0,'2023-05-26 15:21:41','2023-05-26 15:41:47'),(313,721,33,3,0,0,169000,43050,'Hong Kong Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 (26 Jun 2023 - Monday)\r\n* Transfer from Airport to Ferry\r\n* Ferry to Macau\r\n* Transfer to Hotel\r\n* Overnight Stay at Hotel\r\n\r\nDay 2 (27 Jun 2023 - Tuesday)\r\n\r\n* Macau City Tour - ( Ama Temple, Ruins of St Paul Church, Senado Square, Coach View of Macau Tower & Kun Lam Statue) - Max4 Hours\r\n* Overnight Stay at Hotel\r\n\r\nDay 3 (28 Jun 2023 - Wednesday)\r\n\r\n* Transfer to Pier\r\n* Ferry to Hong Kong\r\n* Pickup and Proceed for Victoria Peak, One Way Peak Tram Ride + Old Clock Tower, Victoria Harbour, Night Market - Max 5 Hours\r\n* Overnight Stay at Hotel\r\n\r\nDay 4 (29 Jun 2023 - Thrusday)\r\n\r\n* Ocean park with Return Transfers & entry Ticket\r\n* Overnight stay at Hotel\r\n\r\nDay 5 (30 Jun 2023 - Friday)\r\n\r\n* Disneyland 1-Day Tour with Return Transfers\r\n* Overnight stay at Hotel\r\n\r\nDay 6 (01 Jul 2023 - Saturday)\r\n\r\n* Transfers from Hong Kong Hotel to Airport','','* Economy class return airfare\r\n* Hotel accommodation in Hong Kong and Macua as listed above with Breakfast\r\n* All transfers and Sightseeing\r\n* Travel Insurance','* Meals other than specified in the itinerary.  \r\n* Any expenses of personal nature\r\n* Any services not mentioned in the inclusions list\r\n','The rates are subject to change','2023-06-25','2023-07-01',1,0,0,'2023-05-26 16:14:02','2023-05-26 18:37:10'),(314,722,54,2,0,0,46200,28600,'Singapore Diaries','5 night stay and tour in Singapore','','•	Economy class return airfare\r\n•	Return airport transfers on PVT\r\n•	SIN City Orientation Drive + Afternoon Sentosa\r\n•	Sentosa inclusion (Cable Car + Luge & Skyride + Wings of Time) \r\n•	Night Safari with Tram Ride\r\n•	Universal Studio –  ( Dynamic price excluding CNY period)\r\n•	Gardens by the Bay (Flower Dome + Supertree)\r\n•	Visa Charges\r\n•	Travel Insurance\r\n','* Any meal other than that mentioned above\r\n* Expenditure of a personal nature such as drinks, souvenirs and laundry\r\n* Anything which is not mentioned in the inclusions\r\n* TCS','The airfare is dynamic and subject to change.','2023-07-04','2023-07-09',1,0,0,'2023-05-26 16:55:53','2023-05-26 18:18:38'),(315,723,15595,3,0,0,158800,40800,'Sri Lanka Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 01: Colombo\r\nArrival in Colombo.\r\nRelax and enjoy your first day in Colombo at your own pace.\r\n\r\nDay 02: Colombo - Colombo City Tour / Shopping tour\r\nEmbark on a city tour of Colombo to visit its famous landmarks. Enjoy some shopping in the bustling markets and malls.\r\n\r\nDay 03: Colombo - Explore Colombo Nightlife, Casino, Clubs\r\nExperience the vibrant nightlife of Colombo by visiting popular casinos, clubs, and entertainment venues.\r\n\r\nDay 04: Kandy - Pinnawala Elephant Orphanage / Spice Garden\r\nHead to Kandy and visit the Pinnawala Elephant Orphanage, where you can observe and interact with elephants. Later, explore a spice garden to learn about Sri Lanka\'s aromatic spices.\r\n\r\nDay 05: Kandy - Temple of the Tooth Relic / Royal Botanical Gardens\r\nVisit the Temple of the Tooth Relic, a sacred Buddhist site housing a relic of Lord Buddha\'s tooth. Explore the beautiful Royal Botanical Gardens.\r\n\r\nDay 06: Kandy\r\nEnjoy a day of leisure in Kandy. You can visit local markets, relax in scenic spots, or indulge in optional activities like a traditional Ayurvedic spa treatment.\r\n\r\nDay 07: Bentota - Leisure by the Beach / Water Sports Activities\r\nTravel to Bentota, a coastal town known for its pristine beaches. Spend the day relaxing on the beach or engaging in thrilling water sports activities like jet skiing or banana boat rides.\r\n\r\nDay 08: Bentota - Leisure by the Beach / Water Sports Activities\r\nContinue to enjoy the beach and water sports activities in Bentota.\r\n\r\nDay 09: Bentota - Turtle Hatchery / Madu River Boat Ride\r\nVisit a turtle hatchery to learn about conservation efforts and see adorable baby turtles. Take a scenic boat ride along the Madu River.\r\n\r\nDay 10: Bentota - Leisure\r\nRelax and enjoy your last day in Bentota at your own pace.\r\n\r\n\r\nSupplement Costs:\r\n                    \r\n\r\nPinnawala Elephant Orphanage (US $12 net Rate per person)\r\nTemple of the Tooth Relic (US $10 net Rate per person)\r\nRoyal Botanical Gardens (US $14 net Rate per person)\r\nTurtle Hatchery (US $05 net Rate per person)\r\nMadu River Boat Ride (US $09 net Rate per person)\r\n03 Activity Water sports in Bentota (US $22 net Rate per person)\r\n','','* Accommodation at the above mentioned hotels or similar \r\n* Daily breakfast & dinner at the hotel \r\n* Meet & Assist at the airport \r\n* City tours in Colombo, Kandy & Bentota \r\n* Shopping tour in Colombo \r\n* Drop off to Casino in Colombo.\r\n* An air-conditioned vehicle with an English speaking driver throughout the tour\r\n* All applicable Gov. Taxes   \r\n','* Entrance fees to any sites not mentioned above\r\n* Tips & portages \r\n* Any meals not mentioned above\r\n* Any other services not mentioned above\r\n* Early check in & Late check out\r\n','The rates are subject to change.','2023-07-18','2023-07-29',1,0,0,'2023-05-26 18:02:14','2023-05-27 13:05:35'),(316,724,16159,2,0,0,52100,22000,'Bali-Indonesia','3N Kuta - 2N Seminyak\r\n\r\n\r\nTours includes in Bali :-\r\n* Rafting LONG 12KM with local lunch (Ayung river) with private transfers\r\n* Kintamani tour with Ubud Village + Swing by Pioneer with private transfers\r\n* Nusa Penida tour with transfer and ferry ( 1 point snorkelling day trip) on SIC basis  (Hotel - Bali Port - Hotel - with private transfers)                                                                                                                                            Destination : Broken Beach, Angel Billabong, Klingking Clif & Crystal Bay (1 point Snorkeling)    - Boat start at 08.00 AM and back at 04.00 PM.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              Tour Include : Car for tour island, Driver as Guide, Local Lunch (Vegetarian Only), Return Boat Free entrance all destination, only Snorkeling Equipment, Life Jacket                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 Tour Exclude : Retribution fee to Island Nusa Penida IDR 25.000,-/person.\r\n* Ulundanu Temple of Bedugul Followed by Tanah lot temple tour with private transf