st entry free at Gulmarg & Aru)\r\n* Hotel Taxes\r\n','* Cost of any adventure activities like Gondola Ride, Skiing, Motor Bike, River rafting, Pony / Sledge Ride etc.\r\n* Extra Meals\r\n* Cost of Union Cab services in Pahalgam, Gulmarg and Sonamarg.\r\n* Guide fees, Camera fees, shopping & any monument entrances.\r\n* Guest Entry Fee at Gulmarg / Aru.\r\n* Entrance fee for Mughal Gardens or for any Park/ Museum/Monument.\r\n* Expenses of personal nature such as laundry, mini bars, etc. ','','2023-06-26','2023-07-01',1,0,0,'2023-06-20 16:24:32','2023-06-20 16:24:32'),(355,782,15500,2,0,0,445500,35000,'Europe Package','4N Switzerland - 3N France - 3N Germany\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nSightseeing:\r\nExcursion to Mt Titlis with Swiss Pass\r\nExcursion to Jungfraujoch – Top of Europe With Swiss Pass\r\nZurich City Tour Experience\r\nBig Bus Paris Hop-On-Hop With Eiffel Tower 2 Floor access and Seine River Cruise\r\nLouvre Museum - Skip-the-Line Ticket with Digital Audioguide\r\n\r\n\r\nTrains:\r\nSwiss Pass 04 Days on 2nd Class\r\nTrain From Zurich to Paris on 2nd Class\r\nTrain From Paris to Frankfurt  on 2nd Class\r\n\r\nTransfers:\r\nTransfers From Paris Station to hotel on pvt basis\r\nTransfers From Paris Hotel to Statiojn on pvt basis\r\nTransfers From Frankfurt station to Hotel on pvt basis\r\nTransfers From Frankfurt Hotel to Airport on pvt basis ','','Delhi-Zurich and Frankfurt-Delhi Economy class airfare \r\n11 night stay in above mentioned hotels on breakfast basis\r\nTrain tours as mentioned above\r\nAll transfers and sightseeing as mentioned above\r\nVisa Charges\r\nTravel Insurance\r\n','Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\nAny type of personal expense (like laundary, medical expense, personal grooming etc.)\r\nAnything that is not mentioned in inclusions\r\nTCS','• This is just a quote; no Rooms or Services have been blocked and the same are subject to availability.\r\n• Above rates are valid for Indian National only\r\n• Rates & Availability is subject to change without any prior Notice\r\n•  At most Hotels Standard check-in time will be 1500hrs & checkout will be 1100 hrs .\r\n•  Early check is subject to availability & can incur additional charges.\r\n•  Please check all inclusions as any additions will occur in extra charges.\r\n•  Station / Airport transfers are not included unless mentioned.\r\n• If your Travel period falls during a fair or Event period, A supplement cost will be applicable if any.\r\n• The airfare is dynamic. ','2023-09-13','2023-09-23',1,0,0,'2023-06-21 18:39:38','2023-06-21 18:39:38'),(356,781,15512,3,0,0,227586,45000,'Vietnam Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 – 27 July: Arrival Hanoi Vietnam – City highlights\r\nYour English-speaking guide will meet you at Noi Bai International Airport and welcome you. They will then take you on a city tour, starting with a visit to the beautiful Tran Quoc Pagoda located on the shores of West Lake. Afterward, you will proceed to the Ho Chi Minh complex, which includes Ho Chi Minh\'s Mausoleum (only open in the morning) and his stilt house where he lived from 1958 to 1969. The tour will continue to the One Pillar Pagoda, a unique structure situated in the middle of a square lake. Returning to downtown, you will have a chance to relax by Hoan Kiem Lake and visit Ngoc Son Temple. Finally, you will embark on a walking tour through the Old Quarter, also known as the 36 streets, a vibrant area filled with small businesses and shops. It\'s a fantastic place to explore and capture memorable photos.\r\nCheck in and overnight in Hanoi.\r\n\r\nDay 2 – 28 July: Hanoi – Ninh Binh: Trang An – Bai Dinh Pagoda (B)\r\nAfter breakfast, your guide will meet you at the hotel for a 110km (2-hour) journey through the beautiful countryside. You will arrive at the magnificent Bai Dinh pagoda complex, the largest pagoda in Vietnam and Southeast Asia. Nestled at the foot of Dinh Mountain, the pagoda offers breathtaking views of the surrounding river valley and limestone karsts. In the afternoon, you will visit the Trang An Grottoes, an impressive natural wonder with towering limestone formations spanning 20 square kilometers. Overnight in Hanoi.\r\n\r\nDay 3 – 29 July: Hanoi – Ha Long, welcome on the boat (SIC) (B/L/D)\r\nAt around 8:00 AM, you will depart from your hotel in a private car for a 4-hour journey to Ha Long Bay. Upon arrival at the port around noon, you will be warmly welcomed on board and shown to your cabin. After a trip briefing, you will savor a delicious seafood lunch while cruising through the enchanting Bai Tu Long Bay. There will be a stop for swimming and a visit to a mysterious cave, followed by relaxation at a secluded island beach. In the evening, you will return to the boat in time to witness a stunning sunset from the top deck, followed by a delectable seafood dinner. You will spend the night on the cruise ship.\r\n\r\nDay 4 – 30 July: Explore Bai Tu Long Bay – Hanoi – Da Nang (B/L)\r\nEarly risers can witness the stunning sunrise over the majestic limestone formations of the bay. Breakfast is served at around 8:00 AM, followed by a short rowboat ride guided by the locals. Enjoy brunch on the boat while cruising back to the pier. Return to Hanoi by road.\r\nUpon reaching the center of Hanoi, our driver will pick you up and transfer you to Hanoi airport for your flight to Da Nang. Upon arrival in Da Nang, you will be picked up and transferred to your hotel for check-in. The evening is free for you to relax and explore. Overnight stay in Danang.\r\n\r\nDay 5 – 31 July: Ba Na hill – Golden Bridge full day (B)\r\nAfter breakfast at your hotel, you will be transferred to Ba Na Hills, located 35km from Danang center. Board the Sunworld Cable Car, which has received 5 world records, to reach Ba Na Hills station. Along the way, you will stop at By Night station to visit Vong Nguyet Hills, Linh Ung Pagoda, and the Old Villas of French. Continue ascending to Nui Chua Mountain, the highest peak of the Ba Na range, to explore Nghinh Phong Top, Le Nim Villas, and the Orchid Garden. Experience a unique hill climbing train, visit the flower garden Le Jardin D\'amour, and marvel at the famous Golden Bridge with its panoramic views. Lunch is at your own leisure. In the afternoon, enjoy the various games and attractions at Fantasy Park, the third largest indoor games zone in Vietnam. Around 5pm, return to your hotel.Overnight in Danang.\r\n\r\nDay 6 – 01 Aug: Da Nang - fly to Ho Chi Minh City, city highlights (B)\r\nHave a breakfast at your hotel. Meeting our driver and transfer to the Da Nang airport for flight to Ho Chi Minh. Upon arrival Ho Chi Minh, meeting our driver and transfer to the city downtown (30 minutes) for the city must-not-miss sites including Notre Dame Cathedral, the historic Central Post Office, City Hall, Ben Thanh Market, Nguyen Hue walking boulevard.\r\nHead to your hotel to check in and spend rest of the day at your own leisure.\r\nNote: Check in time 14:00\r\nOvernight in Ho Chi Minh.\r\n\r\nDay 7 – 02 Aug: HCMC – Mekong Delta (B)\r\nt 8:30 AM, you\'ll be picked up for a trip to the Mekong Delta. Board a motorboat in My Tho City to explore canals and observe local life. Visit Thoi Son Island for traditional music, paddle boat rides, coconut candy making, and a bee farm. Enjoy fresh honey and fruits. On the return, visit Vinh Trang Pagoda. Return to Ho Chi Minh City for overnight stay.\r\n\r\nDay 8 – 03 Aug: HCMC departure (B)\r\nBreakfast at hotel. Depending on your flight you may have some more time for shopping by your own. Then we transfer you without guide to the airport for your flight home. Goodbye, and hope to see you again soon!','','* Economy Class airfare.\r\n* Flight Includes Hanoi – Da Nang – Ho Chi Minh.\r\n* Private airport transfer\r\n* Accommodation based on triple sharing room\r\n* Private air-conditioned vehicle with private driver as mentioned itinerary\r\n* Local English speaking guide as mentioned itinerary\r\n* Meals as mentioned (B = breakfast; L = lunch with set menu; D = dinner with set menu)\r\n* SIC tours as mentioned\r\n* Entrance fee to the mentioned itinerary\r\n* Bottled water for the touring day (500ml/bottle/pax/day) \r\n* Private airport transfer\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','* Personal expenses \r\n* TCS','Airafare is dynamic.\r\nThe final cruise itinerary is subject to change based on each cruise’s program.','2023-07-26','2023-08-03',1,0,0,'2023-06-22 14:50:22','2023-06-22 16:02:37'),(357,786,15500,2,0,0,290800,35000,'Europe Package','3N Paris - 3N Switzerland - 3N Germany\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nTrains:\r\nSwiss Pass 04 Days on 2nd Class\r\nTrain ticket  Paris Gare de Lyon  -   Basel  (2nd class)\r\nTrain ticket  Basel  -   Frankfurt am Main Hbf  (2nd class)\r\n\r\nTransfers:\r\nTransfers From Paris Airport to hotel on pvt basis\r\nTransfers From Paris Hotel to Statiojn on pvt basis\r\nTransfers From Frankfurt Hotel to Airport on pvt basis ','','* Delhi-Paris and Frankfurt-Delhi Economy class airfare\r\n* Accommodation\r\n* Daily Breakfast\r\n* Private transfer from Paris Airport to Hotel\r\n* Eiffel Tower Skip the Line Tour & River Cruise with Champagne (Eiffel Tower & Seine River 16:00) (Departure Point) 1 Port de Suffren, 75007 Paris, France\r\n* Versailles Gardens & Palace from Paris with Priority Access (Versailles Gardens & Palace from Paris with Priority Access 10:00)(Departure Point) Javel - André Citroën, 75015 Paris, \r\n* Notre Dame Outdoor Walking Tour with Crypt Entry (Walking Tour in English 13:00) Dep Point: Statue de Charlemagne et ses Leudes, Île de la Cité, 75004 Paris, France\r\n* 04 Days Swiss pass consecutive 2nd Class \r\n* Jungfraujoch with Swiss pass\r\n* Mt. Titlis with Swiss pass\r\n* Rhine Fall with Swiss pass (Entry fee pay locally)\r\n* Train tours as mentioned above\r\n* All transfers and sightseeing as mentioned above\r\n* Visa Charges\r\n* Travel Insurance\r\n','Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\nAny type of personal expense (like laundary, medical expense, personal grooming etc.)\r\nAnything that is not mentioned in inclusions\r\nTCS','• This is just a quote; no Rooms or Services have been blocked and the same are subject to availability.\r\n• Above rates are valid for Indian National only\r\n• Rates & Availability is subject to change without any prior Notice\r\n•  At most Hotels Standard check-in time will be 1500hrs & checkout will be 1100 hrs .\r\n•  Early check is subject to availability & can incur additional charges.\r\n•  Please check all inclusions as any additions will occur in extra charges.\r\n•  Station / Airport transfers are not included unless mentioned.\r\n• If your Travel period falls during a fair or Event period, A supplement cost will be applicable if any.\r\n• The airfare is dynamic. ','2023-09-13','2023-09-22',1,0,0,'2023-06-23 13:44:51','2023-06-23 14:51:04'),(358,787,15526,2,0,0,67400,21000,'Kashmir - the heaven on earth','2N Srinagar - 1N Gulmarg - 1N Pahalgam - 1N Srinagar\r\n\r\n\r\nITINERARY\r\nDay 1 - ARRIVAL + SRINAGAR LOCAL SIGHTSEEING (CHECK-IN HOTEL)\r\n \r\nUpon arrival at Srinagar airport, our representative will meet you to pick you up and transfer you to your hotel. Welcome to Srinagar, the Lake City. Begin your tour of \'Exotic Kashmir. After check-in proceed to Local Sightseeing of Srinagar with a tour of the Mughal Gardens visiting Cheshmashahi (the royal spring), Nishat (the garden of pleasure), Shalimar (the abode of love), and Pari Mahal. Overnight stay at a hotel in Srinagar.\r\n \r\n \r\nDay 2 - SONMARG DAY TRIP  FROM SRINAGAR\r\n \r\nAfter breakfast leave from hotel and proceed to Sonamarg \"Golden Meadow\".  Sonmarg lies in Sind Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. Sonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude of the Himalayan Lakes. Enjoy horse riding up to Thajiwas glacier and sledge riding on snow (own cost). Overnight stay at a hotel in Srinagar.\r\n \r\n \r\nDay 3 - CHECK-IN AT GULMARG (1 NIGHT STAY)\r\n \r\nAfter breakfast leave