joy the backwaters, scenery and different places for 21hrs in Kerala Style House boats from 12Noon. Observe the daily life of peoples who lives near the lake/canal while cruising. In the houseboat you will be greeted with welcome drink. Lunch, Dinner and breakfast will be provided as per the timming. Evening Tea/Coffee & snacks will be provided. Overnight stay in the houseboat.\"\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Royal Rivers Cruises (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 6 (14 Nov 2023 - Tuesday) Alleppey to Kovalam\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Royal Rivers Cruises\r\nTransfers - Alleppey to Kovalam\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel Houseboat and transfer to Kovalam. Check in at Hotel. Kovalam is an evergreen and pleasant climatic beach. Kovalam is a dreamland for tourists all over the world. With high rock promontory and a calm bay of blue waters, this beach paradise creates a unique aquarelle on moonlit nights. Kovalam was brought to the public eye by the Maharaja of Travancore. Over the past three decades, the place has been well developed, and now figures prominently on the world tourism map. Overnight stay at Kovalam.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel SAMUDRATHEERAM (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 7 (15 Nov 2023 - Wednesday) Kovalam – Trivandrum – Kovalam\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - SAMUDRATHEERAM\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Kovalam – Trivandrum – Kovalam\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed for Sightseeing. Visit Padmanabha Swami Temple, Kuthiramalika Palace Museum, Zoo, Napier  Museum & Veli Tourist Village. Overnight stay at Kovalam.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel SAMUDRATHEERAM (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 8 (16 Nov 2023 - Thursday) Trivandrum Dep\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - SAMUDRATHEERAM\r\nDeparture Transfer - Trivandrum Dep\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the Hotel and transferred to Trivandrum Airport/Railway station for your onward journey. Tour ends with happy memories.','','* Meal plans as indicated on the itinerary\r\n* Accommodation on Triple Sharing Basis\r\n* All Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\n* All Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost\r\n','* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Any type of personal expenses\r\n* Anything which is not mentioned in Inclusions\r\n','* Rates are subject to availability\r\n* Airfare is dynamic','2023-11-09','2023-11-16',0,0,0,'2023-06-26 11:52:19','2023-06-26 12:04:13'),(361,793,15530,4,0,0,202400,40000,'Andaman Diaries','\r\n1st Day (10 Nov)\r\nPort Blair Arrival - Cellular Jail – Light & Sound Show (Tickets & Transfers)\r\n\r\n\r\n2nd Day (11 Nov)\r\nPort Blair - North Bay (Coral Island) – Ross Island (Boat charge & Transfers)\r\n\r\n\r\n3rd Day (12 Nov)\r\nPort Blair to Havelock - Radha Nagar Beach\r\nPrivate Catamaran Ferry : Premium\r\n\r\n4th Day (13 Nov)\r\nHavelock - Elephenta Beach (Boat charge & Transfers)\r\n\r\n5th Day (14 Nov)\r\nHavelock to Neil Island - Laxmanpura Beach, Bharatpura Beach & Natural Bridge\r\nPrivate Catamaran Ferry : Premium\r\n\r\n6th Day (15 Nov)\r\nNeil Island to Port Blair - Day at Leisure\r\nPrivate Catamaran Ferry : Premium\r\n\r\n7th Day (16 Nov)\r\nPort Blair Departure - Tour Ends\r\n','','• Delhi-Port Blair -Delhi Economy class airfare\r\n• Meet & Greet services by our local representatives at Airport & Jetty.\r\n• Meal Plan – As mentioned above.\r\n• Airport & Ferry Terminal Transfers in Air-Conditioned Vehicle.\r\n• All Sightseeing (Entry fess included) as per itinerary in Air-Conditioned Vehicle.\r\n• Inter-Island ferry transfers By Private Catamaran Ferries Makruzz (Preferred)/ Nautika/ Green Ocean/ ITT Majestic etc (Subject to Availability)\r\n• 1 Xylo/Ertiga for transfers\r\n','• The services of vehicles not on a disposal basis & finishing the sightseeing tour as per the itinerary\r\n• Any kind of personal expenses or optional tours/extra meals/Vehicles for Dinner etc.','The airfare is dynamic and subject to change. \r\nThe rooms are subject to availability.','2023-11-10','2023-11-16',1,0,0,'2023-06-28 15:29:01','2023-07-03 16:33:04'),(362,794,16260,4,0,0,190700,39000,'Europe Package','2N Lucerne - 2N Interlaken - 1N Zurich\r\n\r\n','','6 Days Swiss Pass\r\n5 Nights accommodation in above mentioned hotels\r\nDaily Breakfast\r\nMt. Titlis Excursion with Swiss Travel Pass incl. Ice Flyer (Return from Engelberg - Mt. Titlis)\r\nJungfraujoch, Train Trip and the Bernese Oberland - Tour\r\nRhine Falls with Swiss Pass (Ferry tickets to be purchased there itself)\r\nZurich City Tour Experience (Start Times 14:00)\r\nAll transfers to be done with swiss pass\r\nTravel Insurance\r\n','Any other meal other than mentioned above\r\nAny excursion other than mentioned above\r\nAny type of personal expense\r\nTCS (5%)\r\n\r\n','The rooms are subject to availability.\r\n\r\nOptional Tour:\r\nChapel Bridge or Lion Monument in Lucerne (Can be done with Swiss Pass)','2023-08-11','2023-08-16',0,0,0,'2023-06-29 14:47:35','2023-06-29 15:17:22'),(363,795,419,2,2,0,86400,19000,'Kashmir Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 - ARRIVAL + SRINAGAR LOCAL SIGHSEEING (CHECK-IN HOTEL)\r\nOn arrival at Srinagar airport, our representative will meet you to pick you up and transfer to your hotel. Welcome to Srinagar, the Lake City. Begin your tour of \'Exotic Kashmir. After check-in proceed to Local Sightseeing of Srinagar with a tour of Mughal Gardens visiting Cheshmashahi (the royal spring), Nishat (the garden of pleasure), Shalimar (the abode of love), Pari Mahal. Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar.\r\n\r\nDay 2 - SONMARG DAY TRIP  FROM SRINAGAR\r\nAfter breakfast leave from hotel and proceed to Sonamarg \"Golden Meadow\".  Sonmarg lies in Sind Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. Sonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude of Himalayan Lakes. Enjoy horse riding upto Thajiwas glacier and sledge riding on snow (own cost). Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar.\r\n\r\nDay 3 - CHECK-IN AT PAHALGAM (1 NIGHT STAY)\r\nAfter breakfast check-out from hotel and transfer to Pahalgam hotel, VILLAGE OF SHEPHERDS “ Pahalgam is known as the land of shepherds. The mountain town is located along the bank of River Lidder. Here you can visit many breath taking places enroute visiting the world famous Saffron  growing  fields . Pahalgam is famous for Indian film industry, some trekking routes & also base camp for Amarnath pilgrimage. One can visit chandanwari,  Betab Valley and Aru Valley (own cost) has a fine Meadows of Picturesque scenery & starting point of trekking of Liddarwat , Kolahoi Glacier , Tarsar Lake. Overnight stay at hotel in Pahalgam.\r\n\r\nDay 4 - CHECK-IN AT GULMARG (1 NIGHT STAY)\r\nAfter breakfast leave from hotel and proceed to Gulmarg . Gulmarg is also known as “Meadow Of Flowers “ & has a famous Golf course during summer  (which is one if the highest 18-holes golf course in the world) & Ski Resort during winter. One can enjoy the breathtaking views of snow clad mountains, Gondola (cable car) ride from Gulmarg to Khilanmarg (own cost) to have a real view in natural beauty of the summer and full snow view in winter. You can have a pony ride in the open fields to seven springs (own cost) and to a lake, which remains frozen until June. Overnight stay at hotel in Gulmarg.\r\n\r\nDay 5 - CHECK-IN AT SRINAGAR HOUSEBOAT\r\nAfter breakfast check-out from hotel and transfer to Srinagar. Upon arrival check-in houseboat. After rest in evening enjoy Shikara Ride on Dal lake for 1 hour and explore the beauty of the lake. Overnight stay at houseboat in Srinagar.\r\n\r\nDay 6 - CHECK-OUT FROM SRINAGAR HOUSEBOAT\r\nAfter breakfast check-out from Srinagar houseboat and transfer to Srinagar Airport to board the flight for onward destination.','','* Delhi-Srinagar-Delhi Economy class airfare\r\n* Accommodation as above.\r\n* Breakfast and Dinner in the hotel.\r\n* Airport - pick-up and drop facility on pvt basis.\r\n* Sightseeing by non-AC vehicle on pvt basis\r\n* Shikara Ride (01 hour) will be given in same houseboat\r\n* Driver Allowances.\r\n* Toll tax and State tax & Parking (Without Guest entry free at Gulmarg & Aru)\r\n* Hotel Taxes\r\n* Vehicle: Etios (NON AC)\r\n','* Cost of any adventure activities like Gondola Ride, Skiing, Motor Bike, River rafting, Pony / Sledge Ride etc.\r\n* Extra Meals\r\n* Cost of Union Cab services in Pahalgam, Gulmarg and Sonamarg.\r\n* Guide fees, Camera fees, shopping & any monument entrances.\r\n* Guest Entry Fee at Gulmarg / Aru.\r\n* Entrance fee for Mughal Gardens or for any Park/ Museum/Monument.\r\n* Expenses of personal nature such as laundry, mini bars, etc. ','Airfare is dynamic','2023-07-28','2023-08-02',1,0,0,'2023-07-01 12:21:41','2023-07-01 12:59:06'),(364,797,15512,2,0,0,155200,26000,'IMPRESSION OF VIETNAM','Day 1 – 10 Aug: Arrival Hanoi Vietnam – City highlights\r\n\r\nUpon arrival at Noi Bai International Airport, meet your tour guide and transfer to the city center. Embark on a city tour starting with a visit to the Ho Chi Minh Mausoleum to learn about the life of Ho Chi Minh, followed by a stop at the One Pillar Pagoda. Explore the Temple of Literature, the oldest university in Vietnam, and stroll through the Hanoi Old Quarter, admiring the French colonial architecture and local shops. Overnight in Hanoi.\r\n\r\nDay 2 – 11 Aug: Hanoi – Ha Long, welcome on the boat (B,L,D)\r\n\r\nDepart from Hanoi in the morning and travel to Ha Long Bay by private van. Arrive at the port, board your cruise, and enjoy a fresh seafood lunch while cruising through Bai Tu Long Bay. Swim, visit a cave, and relax on a secluded island-beach. Watch the sunset from the boat and savor a delicious seafood dinner. Overnight on the cruise.\r\n\r\nDay 3 – 12 Aug: Explore Ha Long Bay – Hanoi – Flight to Da Nang (B,L/Br)\r\n\r\nWake up early to witness the sunrise and the breathtaking beauty of Ha Long Bay. Enjoy breakfast before taking a rowboat ride and having brunch on the cruise. Return to the pier and proceed to the airport for a flight to Da Nang. Overnight in Da Nang.\r\n\r\nDay 4 – 13 Aug: Ba Na Hill – Golden Bridge full day (B)\r\n\r\nVisit Ba Na Hills, taking the Sunworld Cable Car and exploring attractions like Vong Nguyet Hills, Linh Ung Pagoda, and the Old Villas of French. Experience a hill climbing train and admire the Golden Bridge with its panoramic views. Enjoy games at Fantasy Park before returning to your hotel in the afternoon. Overnight in Da Nang.\r\n\r\nDay 5 – 14 Aug: Da Nang - Fly to Ho Chi Minh City, city highlights (B)\r\n\r\nFly from Da Nang to Ho Chi Minh City. Start your city tour with a visit to downtown HCM City and the bustling Binh Tay Market. Stop at Thien Hau Temple and explore a lacquer-wares workshop and the Jade Emperor Pagoda. Visit the Notre Dame Cathedral and the Central Post Office. Return to your hotel after the tour. Overnight in Ho Chi Minh City.\r\n\r\nDay 6 – 15 Aug: Cu Chi Tunnel – Ho Chi Minh Departure (B)\r\n\r\nDepart for the Cu Chi Tunnels, where you\'ll learn about their construction and the survival tactics employed during the war. Explore the tunnel systems, experience guerilla life, and taste tea and cassava. Optionally, try shooting a real gun. Afterward, relax before being transferred to the airport for your departure.\r\n\r\nNote: This itinerary includes private transfers, guides, entrance fees, accommodation, and meals as specified. The final cruise itinerary is subject to change based on each cruise\'s program.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDomestic Flights:\r\n12 AUG: HAN – DAD (20:15 – 21:35)\r\n14 AUG: DAD – SGN (09:00 - 10:25)\r\n\r\n','','* Delhi-Hanoi and Ho Chi Minh - Delhi Economy class airfare \r\n* Accommodation based on twin/double sharing room\r\n* Private air-conditioned vehicle with private driver as mentioned itinerary\r\n* Local English speaking guide as mentioned itinerary\r\n* Meals as mentioned (B = breakfast; L = lunch with set menu; D = dinner with set menu)\r\n* SIC tours as mentioned\r\n* Entrance fee t