nTravel Insurance - recommended.  We request Tour Operator to secure a signed Waiver in the event client declines your offer to sell Travel Insurance\r\nAny items not mentioned in Package inclusions column  ','Rooms are subject to availability\r\nHotel / Coach Station / Hotel transfers to be managed on own.','2024-05-15','2024-05-20',0,0,0,'2023-12-05 21:53:15','2023-12-05 21:53:15'),(486,982,16002,2,0,0,37500,15000,'Glimpse of Bali','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1: Arrival & transfer to hotel with private transfers\r\nArrive in Bali and transfer to your hotel with private transportation. This is likely a day for rest and settling in.\r\n\r\nDay 2: Water Sports Activity + Uluwatu Temple with private transfers\r\n\r\n* Engage in water sports activities such as Jet Ski, Banana Boat, and Single Parasailing (subject to availability).\r\n* Visit Uluwatu Temple with private transfers. This temple is known for its stunning location on a cliff overlooking the Indian Ocean.\r\n\r\nDay 3: 02 Hrs Bali Spa @ Grand Inna Kuta + Tanah Lot Temple with private transfers\r\n\r\n* Enjoy a 2-hour spa session at Grand Inna Kuta for relaxation.\r\n* Visit Tanah Lot Temple, a beautiful sea temple located on a rock formation in the ocean.\r\n\r\nDay 4: Ubud & Kintamani + Bali Swing Pioneer with private transfers + Interhotel\r\n\r\n* Explore Ubud and Kintamani, known for their cultural and scenic attractions.\r\n* Experience the Bali Swing Pioneer.\r\n* Transfer to another hotel (Interhotel).\r\n\r\nDay 5: Leisure\r\nThis day seems to be free for leisure, allowing for flexibility in your plans. You can explore more on your own or relax at the hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 6: Departure with private transfers\r\nDepart from Bali with private transportation to the airport.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nEnjoy your trip to Bali!','','* Economy class airfare.\r\n* 05 Nights Accommodation as per above with breakfast basis\r\n* Return airport transfers on pvt basis\r\n* All tours and sightseeings in pvt basis\r\n* Travel Insurance.\r\n','* TCS','Airfare is dynamic.','2024-01-21','2024-01-26',1,0,0,'2023-12-11 15:53:46','2023-12-11 16:29:15'),(487,983,15510,2,0,0,24300,13000,'Thailand Diaries','','','* Economy class airfare\r\n* 05 Nights Accommodation as per above with breakfast basis\r\n* 3 way transfers from BKK airport (Suvarnabhumi) to Pattaya hotel to Bangkok hotel to Bkk airport PVT basis\r\n* Pattaya City Tour + Gems Gallery without guide PVT basis\r\n* Coral Island Tour by Speedboat with Indian Buffet Lunch (PU/ 09:00AM) SIC basis\r\n* Alcazar Show with Transfers + 1 Soft Drink (Normal Seat) (Evening) (ADT/CHD Rate is Same) PVT basis\r\n* Full Day Safari World + Marine Park with Lunch (PU/ 08:00AM) SIC basis\r\n* Travel Insurance','TCS','Airfare is dynamic.','2024-01-21','2024-01-26',1,0,0,'2023-12-11 16:51:31','2023-12-11 17:14:36'),(488,984,419,4,0,0,0,0,'Kashmir Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 : ARRIVE SRINAGAR – GULMARG - OVERNIGHT STAY IN GULMARG\r\nUpon arrival you will be met by our representative at the Srinagar Airport , He will assist you and transfer you to Gulmarg , Gulmarg (Meadow of Flowers) 2730 mts. above the sea level. The distance of 60 kms will be covered in about 2 hours. Gulmarg has one of the best ski slopes in the world and highest golf course with 18 holes. If weather permits one can also have the view of Nanga Parbat, the naked mountain that is over 26,000 feets and dominates the entire region, also enjoy cable car (Gondola) for mountain ride upto khilangmarg. Dinner and overnight in hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : GULMARG TO SRINAGAR\r\nAfter breakfast drive back to Srinagar. sightseeing of the Mughal Gardens, visiting Nishat Bagh built by Asaf Khan, the brother -in- law of Jehangir in 1632 AD, and Shalimar Bagh built by Jehangir for his wife empress Nur Jahan. All the gardens are situated on the banks of the Dal Lake with the Zabarwan hills in the background. Afternoon will be at your leisure for individual activities. Dinner and overnight in hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 3 : DAY TRIP TO PAHALGAM\r\nAfter breakfast drive to Pahalgam (The valley of shepherds).The total distance is about 96 kms, will be covered in about 3 hours. En-route, visiting the saffron fields of pampore, Awantipura Ruins (1100 years old temple of Lord Vishnu built by the King Awantivarman), and enjoy the beautiful countryside.Drive throught the pine forests. Arrive at Pahalgam and enjoy Lidder stream. Later walk along pony trails with a magnificent view of the mountains.Drive back to Srinagar. Overnight in hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 4 : DAY TRIP TO SONMARG\r\nMorning proceed for Sonmarg (Meadow of Gold). The distance of about 83 kms, will be covered in about 3 hrs. Sonmarg lies in Sindh Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. Sonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude Himalayan Lakes. In the evening drive back from Sonmarg. Dinner and overnight in deluxe houseboat\r\n\r\nDay 5 : DEPARTURE FROM SRINAGAR HOTEL TO SRINAGAR AIRPORT\r\nAfter breakfast transfer to Srinagar airport for onward flight.\r\n','','* Economy class airfare.\r\n* Meal Plan: MAPAI (Room + Breakfast + Dinner )\r\n* 01 Shikara Ride.\r\n* Sightseeing as per the itinerary.\r\n* All Arrival/Departure transfer as mentioned in Itinerary.\r\n* 1 Non Ac Sedan (PVT)','* Mineral water / Soft or hard drinks / Starters.                                                                                                 * Entrance Free\r\n* Room Heating Charges in Houseboats\r\n* Horse Riding\r\n* Sightseeing of Chandanwadi, Aru and Baisaran in Pahalgam.\r\n* Gondola Ride in Gulmarg\r\n* Any other things that is not included in the Package\r\n','Airfare is dynamic.','2023-12-29','2024-01-02',1,0,0,'2023-12-12 13:14:17','2023-12-14 16:18:53'),(489,985,16002,2,0,0,48200,18000,'Glimpse of Bali','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1: Arrival & transfer to hotel with private transfers\r\nArrive in Bali and transfer to your hotel with private transportation. This is likely a day for rest and settling in.\r\n\r\nDay 2: Water Sports Activity + Uluwatu Temple with private transfers\r\n\r\n* Engage in water sports activities such as Jet Ski, Banana Boat, and Single Parasailing (subject to availability).\r\n* Visit Uluwatu Temple with private transfers. This temple is known for its stunning location on a cliff overlooking the Indian Ocean.\r\n\r\nDay 3: 02 Hrs Bali Spa @ Grand Inna Kuta + Tanah Lot Temple with private transfers\r\n\r\n* Enjoy a 2-hour spa session at Grand Inna Kuta for relaxation.\r\n* Visit Tanah Lot Temple, a beautiful sea temple located on a rock formation in the ocean.\r\n\r\nDay 4: Ubud & Kintamani + Bali Swing Pioneer with private transfers + Interhotel\r\n\r\n* Explore Ubud and Kintamani, known for their cultural and scenic attractions.\r\n* Experience the Bali Swing Pioneer.\r\n* Transfer to another hotel (Interhotel).\r\n\r\nDay 5: Leisure\r\nThis day seems to be free for leisure, allowing for flexibility in your plans. You can explore more on your own or relax at the hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 6: Departure with private transfers\r\nDepart from Bali with private transportation to the airport.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nEnjoy your trip to Bali!','','* Economy class airfare.\r\n* 05 Nights Accommodation as per above with breakfast basis\r\n* Return airport transfers on pvt basis\r\n* All tours and sightseeings in pvt basis\r\n* Travel Insurance.\r\n','* TCS','Airfare is dynamic.','2024-01-21','2024-01-26',1,0,0,'2023-12-13 18:32:18','2023-12-13 18:36:31'),(490,986,419,4,0,0,0,0,'Kashmir Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 : ARRIVE SRINAGAR – GULMARG - OVERNIGHT STAY IN GULMARG\r\nUpon arrival you will be met by our representative at the Srinagar Airport , He will assist you and transfer you to Gulmarg , Gulmarg (Meadow of Flowers) 2730 mts. above the sea level. The distance of 60 kms will be covered in about 2 hours. Gulmarg has one of the best ski slopes in the world and highest golf course with 18 holes. If weather permits one can also have the view of Nanga Parbat, the naked mountain that is over 26,000 feets and dominates the entire region, also enjoy cable car (Gondola) for mountain ride upto khilangmarg. Dinner and overnight in hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : GULMARG TO SRINAGAR\r\nAfter breakfast drive back to Srinagar. sightseeing of the Mughal Gardens, visiting Nishat Bagh built by Asaf Khan, the brother -in- law of Jehangir in 1632 AD, and Shalimar Bagh built by Jehangir for his wife empress Nur Jahan. All the gardens are situated on the banks of the Dal Lake with the Zabarwan hills in the background. Afternoon will be at your leisure for individual activities. Dinner and overnight in hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 3 : DAY TRIP TO PAHALGAM\r\nAfter breakfast drive to Pahalgam (The valley of shepherds).The total distance is about 96 kms, will be covered in about 3 hours. En-route, visiting the saffron fields of pampore, Awantipura Ruins (1100 years old temple of Lord Vishnu built by the King Awantivarman), and enjoy the beautiful countryside.Drive throught the pine forests. Arrive at Pahalgam and enjoy Lidder stream. Later walk along pony trails with a magnificent view of the mountains.Drive back to Srinagar. Overnight in hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 4 : DAY TRIP TO SONMARG\r\nMorning proceed for Sonmarg (Meadow of Gold). The distance of about 83 kms, will be covered in about 3 hrs. Sonmarg lies in Sindh Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. Sonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude Himalayan Lakes. In the evening drive back from Sonmarg. Dinner and overnight in deluxe houseboat\r\n\r\nDay 5 : DEPARTURE FROM SRINAGAR HOTEL TO SRINAGAR AIRPORT\r\nAfter breakfast transfer to Srinagar airport for onward flight.\r\n','','* Economy class airfare.\r\n* Meal Plan: MAPAI (Room + Breakfast + Dinner )\r\n* 01 Shikara Ride.\r\n* Sightseeing as per the itinerary.\r\n* All Arrival/Departure transfer as mentioned in Itinerary.\r\n* 1 Non Ac Sedan (PVT)','* Mineral water / Soft or hard drinks / Starters.                                                                                                 * Entrance Free\r\n* Room Heating Charges in Houseboats\r\n* Horse Riding\r\n* Sightseeing of Chandanwadi, Aru and Baisaran in Pahalgam.\r\n* Gondola Ride in Gulmarg\r\n* Any other things that is not included in the Package\r\n','Airfare is dynamic.','2023-12-29','2024-01-02',1,0,0,'2023-12-14 16:30:03','2023-12-14 16:30:03'),(491,987,16002,2,0,0,81650,20000,'Glimpse of Bali','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1: Arrival & transfer to hotel with private transfers\r\nArrive in Bali and transfer to your hotel with private transportation. This is likely a day for rest and settling in.\r\n\r\nDay 2: Water Sports Activity + Uluwatu Temple with private transfers\r\n\r\n* Engage in water sports activities such as Jet Ski, Banana Boat, and Single Parasailing (subject to availability).\r\n* Visit Uluwatu Temple with private transfers. This temple is known for its stunning location on a cliff overlooking the Indian Ocean.\r\n\r\nDay 3: 02 Hrs Bali Spa @ Grand Inna Kuta + Tanah Lot Temple with private transfers\r\n\r\n* Enjoy a 2-hour spa session at Grand Inna Kuta for relaxation.\r\n* Visit Tanah Lot Temple, a beautiful sea temple located on a rock formation in the ocean.\r\n\r\nDay 4: Ubud & Kintamani + Bali Swing Pioneer with private transfers + Interhotel\r\n\r\n* Explore Ubud and Kintamani, known for their cultural and scenic attractions.\r\n* Experience the Bali Swing Pioneer.\r\n* Transfer to another hotel (Interhotel).\r\n\r\nDay 5: Leisure\r\nThis day seems to be free for leisure, allowing for flexibility in your plans. You can explore more on your own or relax at the hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 6: Departure with private transfers\r\nDepart from Bali with private transportation to the airport.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nEnjoy your trip to Bali!','','* Economy class airfare.\r\n* 05 Nights Accommodation as per above with breakfast basis\r\n* Return airport transfers on pvt basis\r\n* All tours and sightseeings in pvt basis\r\n* Travel Insurance.\r\n','* TCS','Airfare is dynamic.','2024-01-21','2024-01-26',1,0,0,'2023-12-16 12:55:17','2023-12-16 13:25:10'),(492,989,1616,4,1,0,68000,13000,'Tirupati Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 (23 Jan 2024 - Tuesday) Arrival Chennai - Tirupathi \r\nMeet & Assist on arrival\r\nArrival Transfer - Arrival Chennai - Tirupathi\r\nOn arrival at the Chennai airport/railway station, meet our representative who will be there for your warm welcome and afterwards to transfer you to Tirupati. Tirupati is a city in the Indian state of Andhra Pradesh. Its Sri Venkateswara Temple sits atop one of the the 7 peaks of Tirumala Hills, attracting scores of Hindu pilgrims. Sri Venkateswara National Park, home to the temple, also contains the Sri Venkateswara Zoological Park with lions and primates. Nearby, next to a waterfall and cave believed to be sacred, Sri Kapileswara Swamy Temple is dedicated to Lord Shiva. Check in at the hotel and the rest of the day is free at leisure. During your free time, you can walk out to explore the surroundings, interact with locals, visit local markets or stay back in hotel to take pleasure of its modern amenities. \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Starlit Suites Tirupati(Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 2 (24 Jan 2024 - Wednesday) Tirupati to Tirupathi Sightseeing Day 02 \r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Starlit Suites Tirupati\r\nMorning after breakfast local sightseeing of temples in Tirupati including Sri Govindarajaswami Temple, Kapila Theertham, Padmavati Temple, Trimala (Tirupati Balaji) Temple Akash Ganga & Paap Vinashni Temple.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Starlit Suites Tirupati (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 3 (25 Jan 2024 - Thursday)  Tirupathi  Day 03 \r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Starlit Suites Tirupati\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Starlit Suites Tirupati (Option 1) (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 4 (26 Jan 2024 - Friday) Chennai Departure \r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Starlit Suites Tirupati\r\nDeparture Transfer - Chennai Departure\r\nMorning after breakfast check out the Hotel and drive towards the Chennai international Airport/Railway station for your onward journey. Tour ends with happy memories. ','','* Economy class airfare.\r\n* Meal plans as indicated on the itinerary \r\n* Tirumala Special Darshan\r\n* All Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM \r\n* All Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost \r\n\r\n','* All those which are not mentioned above\r\n* Entry Fees To Monuments And Palaces\r\n* Porterage At Hotels And Airports, Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Liquors, Wine, Etc\r\n* All Items Of Personal Nature\r\n* Any Cost Arising Due To Natural Calamities Like Landslides, Roadblocks, Etc','Airfare is dynamic.','2024-01-23','2024-01-26',1,0,0,'2023-12-19 17:50:30','2023-12-19 18:22:58'),(493,990,1616,4,1,0,68000,13000,'Tirupati Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 (23 Jan 2024 - Tuesday) Arrival Chennai - Tirupathi \r\nMeet & Assist on arrival\r\nArrival Transfer - Arrival Chennai - Tirupathi\r\nOn arrival at the Chennai airport/railway station, meet our representative who will be there for your warm welcome and afterwards to transfer you to Tirupati. Tirupati is a city in the Indian state of Andhra Pradesh. Its Sri Venkateswara Temple sits atop one of the the 7 peaks of Tirumala Hills, attracting scores of Hindu pilgrims. Sri Venkateswara National Park, home to the temple, also contains the Sri Venkateswara Zoological Park with lions and primates. Nearby, next to a waterfall and cave believed to be sacred, Sri Kapileswara Swamy Temple is dedicated to Lord Shiva. Check in at the hotel and the rest of the day is free at leisure. During your free time, you can walk out to explore the surroundings, interact with locals, visit local markets or stay back in hotel to take pleasure of its modern amenities. \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Starlit Suites Tirupati(Meal Plan - CPAI)