alifa (124th) normal entry ticket on SIC basis \r\n\r\nDay 4: Free For leisure\r\n\r\nDay 5: Abu Dhabi City Tour (without lunch on sharing basis)\r\n\r\nDay 6: Departure Airport Transfer from Bur Dubai  hotel to Dubai International Airport (Terminal 1/2/3) on Private Basis','','Delhi-Dubai-Delhi Economy Class airfare\r\nAccommodation in above mentioned hotel with daily breakfast\r\nTransfers and sightseeing as mentioned above on private or sharing basis\r\nTravel Insurance\r\nVisa Charges\r\n','Anything that is not mentioned above\r\nAny meal other than mentioned above\r\n20% TCS','Airfare is dynamic\r\nThe rooms are subject to availability','2024-01-07','2024-01-12',1,0,0,'2023-12-21 14:52:14','2023-12-21 14:52:14'),(495,993,15783,4,0,0,160000,24000,'Jaisalmer-Jodhpur','Day-wise Itinerary:\r\n\r\n1st Day (Thu 28th December) : Jaisalmer - Arrival\r\n\r\nArrival at jaisalmer airport and Transfer to Hotel\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n2nd Day (Fri 29th December) : Jaisalmer to Sam Sand Dunes - Sightseeing and Evening at Sand Dunes\r\n\r\nApprox Distance: 45 Km\r\n\r\nAfter Breakfast at the Hotel, Check out from the Hotel, Take a transfer to the Sam Sand Dunes – 45 km away, Arrival & check into tents, Sam Dunes is known for its sand rises and is the scene for the Desert celebration, Get the genuine feel of the desert by getting a charge out of a camel ride on the sand rises and witness a brilliant nightfall, After enjoying the rides, enjoy the cultural programme, Dinner & Overnight stay in Tents.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n3rd Day (Sat 30th December) : Sam Sand Dunes to Jodhpur - Transfer and Sightseeing\r\n\r\nApprox Distance: 300 Km\r\n\r\nAfter Breakfast check-out from the Tent and Drive to Jodhpur, Check in at the hotel, Jodhpur is a beautiful city that displays the rich crafts and culture of Rajasthan, Head out for sightseeing at the popular forts and Lakes here, Visit Jaswant Thada, This is a marble cenotaph built in 1899, in remembrance of Maharaja Jaswant Singh II, And then head to Mehrangarh Fort, Rising opposite and secure from a slope which is 125 meters over Jodhpur’s horizon is the Mehrangarh Fort, This memorable fortification is a standout amongst the most well known in India and is stuffed with history and legends, Mehrangarh Fort still bears the engravings of cannonball assaults used by the armed forces of Jaipur on its second entryway, (if time permits) Or you can also visit the local market for shopping or wander the streets on your own, Later back to Hotel, Dinner & Overnight stay at Jodhpur Hotel.\r\n\r\n\r\n4th Day (Sun 31st December) : Jodhpur - Sightseeing\r\n\r\nApprox Distance: 100 Km\r\n\r\nAfter breakfast, head out for sightseeing at the popular forts and Lakes here,Visit Jaswant Thada,This is a marble cenotaph built in 1899, in remembrance of Maharaja Jaswant Singh II, And then head to Mehrangarh Fort,Rising opposite and secure from a slope which is 125 meters over Jodhpur’s horizon is the Mehrangarh Fort,This memorable fortification is a standout amongst the most well known in India and is stuffed with history and legends,Mehrangarh Fort still bears the engravings of cannonball assaults used by the armed forces of Jaipur on its second entryway,Also visit Moti Mahal,Moti Mahal, as the name proposes, is the Pearl Hall where the illustrious families held their group of onlookers,The corridor is known to have glass windows and five niches that empowered the rulers to tune in to the procedures occurring in the Sringar Chowki, The Royal Throne of Jodhpur,Later get back to Hotel,Dinner & Overnight stay at Jodhpur Hotel.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n5th Day (Mon 1st January) : Jodhpur - Departure\r\n\r\nApprox Distance: 20 Km\r\n\r\nAfter Breakfast check-out from the Hotel and take a transfer to JODHPUR Airport','','Delhi-Jaisalmer and Jodhpur-Delhi Economy Class Airport\r\nWelcome Drink on Arrival\r\nAccommodation in a well-appointed room in base category\r\nMeals as Mentioned in Hotel Section\r\nHotel checks in & check out time as per the hotel policy\r\nToyota Innova for all transfers and sightseeing\r\nCamel ride and cultural evening at Sam Sand dunes.','Any meal other than the mentioned above.\r\nAll personal expenses, optional tours and extra meal\r\nAny monument or sight-seeing Entry fee / Charges\r\nAnything not in inclusions is excluded','The airfare is dynamic\r\nThe rooms are subject to availability','2023-12-28','2024-01-01',1,0,0,'2023-12-26 17:49:23','2023-12-26 17:49:23'),(496,994,15783,3,0,0,161500,22000,'Jaisalmer-Jodhpur','Day-wise Itinerary:\r\n\r\n1st Day (Thu 28th December) : Jaisalmer - Arrival\r\n\r\nArrival at jaisalmer airport and Transfer to Hotel\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n2nd Day (Fri 29th December) : Jaisalmer to Sam Sand Dunes - Sightseeing and Evening at Sand Dunes\r\n\r\nApprox Distance: 45 Km\r\n\r\nAfter Breakfast at the Hotel, Check out from the Hotel, Take a transfer to the Sam Sand Dunes – 45 km away, Arrival & check into tents, Sam Dunes is known for its sand rises and is the scene for the Desert celebration, Get the genuine feel of the desert by getting a charge out of a camel ride on the sand rises and witness a brilliant nightfall, After enjoying the rides, enjoy the cultural programme, Dinner & Overnight stay in Tents.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n3rd Day (Sat 30th December) : Sam Sand Dunes to Jodhpur - Transfer and Sightseeing\r\n\r\nApprox Distance: 300 Km\r\n\r\nAfter Breakfast check-out from the Tent and Drive to Jodhpur, Check in at the hotel, Jodhpur is a beautiful city that displays the rich crafts and culture of Rajasthan, Head out for sightseeing at the popular forts and Lakes here, Visit Jaswant Thada, This is a marble cenotaph built in 1899, in remembrance of Maharaja Jaswant Singh II, And then head to Mehrangarh Fort, Rising opposite and secure from a slope which is 125 meters over Jodhpur’s horizon is the Mehrangarh Fort, This memorable fortification is a standout amongst the most well known in India and is stuffed with history and legends, Mehrangarh Fort still bears the eng